#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:95
msgid "HTML tags"
msgstr "HTML tag'lar"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:97
msgid ""
"It may seem obvious, but the simplest and most **consistent** way of making "
"text look like a title is to use a header tag (`<h1>`, `<h2>`, ...). Besides "
"reboot rules, mostly all tags carry decorative styles defined by Odoo."
msgstr ""
"Bu aniq ko'rinishi mumkin, ammo matnni sarlavhaga o'xshatishning eng oddiy "
"va eng **izchil** usuli — header tag'dan foydalanish (`<h1>`, `<h2>`, ...). "
"Reboot qoidalaridan tashqari, deyarli barcha tag'lar Odoo tomonidan "
"belgilangan dekorativ style'larga ega."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:106
msgid "Don't"
msgstr "Bunday qilmang"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:138
msgid "Do"
msgstr "Bunday qiling"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:163
msgid ""
"Besides reducing the amount of code, a modular-design approach (use classes, "
"tags, mixins...) keeps the visual result consistent and easily "
"**maintainable**."
msgstr ""
"Kod hajmini kamaytirishdan tashqari, modulli dizayn yondashuvi (class'lar, "
"tag'lar, mixin'lardan foydalanish...) vizual natijani izchil va oson "
"**qo'llab-quvvatlanadigan** holda saqlaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:166
msgid ""
"Following the last example, if Odoo titles' design changes, these changes "
"will be applied in the `o_module_custom_title` element too since it's using "
"an `<h5>` tag."
msgstr ""
"Oxirgi misolga ko'ra, agar Odoo sarlavhalarining dizayni o'zgarsa, bu "
"o'zgarishlar `o_module_custom_title` elementiga ham qo'llaniladi, chunki u "
"`<h5>` tag'idan foydalanadi."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:172
msgid "Utility classes"
msgstr "Utility class'lar"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:174
msgid ""
"Our framework defines a multitude of utility classes designed to cover "
"almost all layout/design/interaction needs. The simple fact that a class "
"already exists justifies its use over custom CSS whenever possible."
msgstr ""
"Bizning framework deyarli barcha layout/dizayn/interaksiya ehtiyojlarini "
"qoplash uchun mo'ljallangan ko'plab utility class'larni aniqlaydi. Class "
"allaqachon mavjud bo'lishining o'zi imkon bo'lgan har qanday holatda uni "
"maxsus CSS o'rniga ishlatishni oqlaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:178
msgid "Take the example of `position-relative`."
msgstr "`position-relative` misolini olib ko'ring."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:186
msgid ""
"Since a utility-class is defined, any CSS line with the declaration "
"`position: relative` is **potentially** redundant."
msgstr ""
"Utility class allaqachon aniqlangani uchun, `position: relative` "
"deklaratsiyasiga ega har qanday CSS qatori **ehtimol** ortiqchadir."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:189
msgid ""
"Odoo relies on the default `Bootstrap utility-classes <https://"
"getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/utilities/background/>`_ stack and defines its own "
"using `Bootstrap API <https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/utilities/api/>`_."
msgstr ""
"Odoo standart `Bootstrap utility-classes <https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/"
"utilities/background/>`_ to'plamiga tayanadi va `Bootstrap API <https://"
"getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/utilities/api/>`_ yordamida o'zining utility "
"class'larini aniqlaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:194
msgid ""
"`Bootstrap utility classes <https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/utilities/api/"
">`_"
msgstr ""
"`Bootstrap utility class'lari <https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/utilities/"
"api/>`_"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:195
msgid ""
"`Odoo custom utilities on github <https://github.com/odoo/odoo/blob/19.0/"
"addons/web/static/src/scss/utilities_custom.scss>`_"
msgstr ""
"`Odoo maxsus utility'lari github'da <https://github.com/odoo/odoo/blob/19.0/"
"addons/web/static/src/scss/utilities_custom.scss>`_"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:201
msgid "Handling utility-classes verbosity"
msgstr "Utility class'larning ortiqcha uzunligini boshqarish"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:203
msgid "The downside of utility-classes is the potential lack of readability."
msgstr "Utility class'larning kamchiligi — o'qilishi qiyinlashishi ehtimoli."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:214
msgid "To overcome the issue you may combine different approaches:"
msgstr ""
"Bu muammoni hal qilish uchun turli yondashuvlarni birlashtirishingiz mumkin:"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:216
msgid "in Qweb attributes, only use classes to be toggled *on-the-fly*;"
msgstr ""
"Qweb attribute'larida faqat *on-the-fly* almashtiriladigan class'lardan "
"foydalaning;"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:217
msgid "use new lines for each attribute;"
msgstr "har bir attribute uchun yangi qatordan foydalaning;"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:218
msgid ""
"order classes using the convention `[odoo component] [bootstrap component] "
"[css declaration order]`."
msgstr ""
"class'larni `[odoo component] [bootstrap component] [css declaration order]` "
"konventsiyasiga muvofiq tartiblang."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/scss_tips.rst:233
msgid ""
":ref:`Odoo CSS properties order <contributing/coding_guidelines/scss/"
"properties_order>`"
msgstr ""
":ref:`Odoo CSS xossalarining tartibi <contributing/coding_guidelines/scss/"
"properties_order>`"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:5
msgid ""
"For any number of reasons, you may want to have a standalone Owl application "
"that isn't a part of the web client. One example in Odoo is the self-"
"ordering application, that lets customers order food from their phone. In "
"this chapter we will go into what's required to achieve something like this."
msgstr ""
"Turli sabablarga ko'ra sizga web client'ning bir qismi bo'lmagan mustaqil "
"(standalone) Owl application kerak bo'lishi mumkin. Odoo'dagi misollardan "
"biri — mijozlarga telefonidan ovqat buyurtma qilish imkonini beruvchi o'zini-"
"o'zi xizmat qilish (self-ordering) application. Bu bo'limda bunday natijaga "
"erishish uchun nima talab qilinishini ko'rib chiqamiz."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:12
msgid "To have a standalone Owl app, a few things are required:"
msgstr "Mustaqil Owl app yaratish uchun bir nechta narsa talab qilinadi:"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:14
msgid "a root component for the application"
msgstr "application uchun root component"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:15
msgid "an assets bundle that contains the setup code"
msgstr "sozlash (setup) kodini o'z ichiga olgan assets bundle"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:16
msgid "a QWeb view that calls the assets bundle"
msgstr "assets bundle'ni chaqiruvchi QWeb view"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:17
msgid "a controller that renders the view"
msgstr "view'ni render qiluvchi controller"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:20
msgid "1. Root component"
msgstr "1. Root component"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:25
msgid ""
"First, create the template in :file:`/your_module/static/src/standalone_app/"
"root.xml`."
msgstr ""
"Avvalo, :file:`/your_module/static/src/standalone_app/root.xml` faylida "
"template yarating."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:36
msgid ""
"Then create the JavaScript file for that component in :file:`/your_module/"
"static/src/standalone_app/root.js`."
msgstr ""
"So'ngra ushbu component uchun JavaScript faylini :file:`/your_module/static/"
"src/standalone_app/root.js` da yarating."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:47
msgid ""
"It's generally a good idea to have the application setup code that mounts "
"the component in a separate file. Create the JavaScript file that will mount "
"the app in :file:`/your_module/static/src/standalone_app/app.js`."
msgstr ""
"Component'ni mount qiluvchi application setup kodini alohida faylda saqlash "
"odatda yaxshi yechim. App'ni mount qiladigan JavaScript faylini :file:`/"
"your_module/static/src/standalone_app/app.js` da yarating."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:58
msgid ""
"The `mountComponent` utility function will take care of creating the Owl "
"application and configuring it correctly: it will create an environment, "
"start the :ref:`services<frontend/services>`, make sure the app is "
"translated and give the app access to the templates from your assets bundle, "
"among other things."
msgstr ""
"`mountComponent` yordamchi funksiyasi Owl application'ni yaratish va uni "
"to'g'ri sozlash bilan shug'ullanadi: u environment "
"yaratadi, :ref:`services<frontend/services>` ni ishga tushiradi, app tarjima "
"qilinganiga ishonch hosil qiladi va app'ga sizning assets bundle'ingizdagi "
"template'larga kirish imkonini beradi, va boshqalar."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:68
msgid "2. Creating an assets bundle containing our code"
msgstr "2. Kodimizni o'z ichiga olgan assets bundle yaratish"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:70
msgid ""
"In the manifest of your module, create a new :ref:`assets bundle<reference/"
"assets_bundle>`. It should include the `web._assets_core` bundle, which "
"contains the Odoo JavaScript framework and the core libraries it needs (e.g. "
"Owl and luxon), after which you can have a glob that adds all the files for "
"your application in the bundle."
msgstr ""
"Modulingiz manifest'ida yangi :ref:`assets bundle<reference/assets_bundle>` "
"yarating. U Odoo JavaScript framework'ini va unga kerakli asosiy "
"kutubxonalarni (masalan Owl va luxon) o'z ichiga olgan `web._assets_core` "
"bundle'ini qo'shishi kerak; shundan keyin application'ingizning barcha "
"fayllarini bundle'ga qo'shadigan glob yozishingiz mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:92
msgid ""
"The other lines are bundles and scss files that are required to make "
"Bootstrap work. They are mandatory, as the components of the web framework "
"use bootstrap classes for their styling and layout."
msgstr ""
"Qolgan qatorlar — Bootstrap ishlashi uchun zarur bo'lgan bundle'lar va scss "
"fayllar. Ular majburiy, chunki web framework component'lari styling va "
"layout uchun bootstrap class'laridan foydalanadi."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:97
msgid ""
"Make sure that the files for your standalone app are only added to this "
"bundle, if you already have a definition for `web.assets_backend` or "
"`web.assets_frontend` and they have globs, make sure these globs don't match "
"the files for your standalone app, otherwise the startup code for your app "
"will conflict with the existing startup code in those bundles."
msgstr ""
"Mustaqil app'ingizning fayllari faqat shu bundle'ga qo'shilganiga ishonch "
"hosil qiling. Agar sizda allaqachon `web.assets_backend` yoki "
"`web.assets_frontend` ta'rifi bo'lsa va ularda glob'lar bo'lsa, bu glob'lar "
"mustaqil app'ingiz fayllariga mos kelmasligini tekshiring, aks holda "
"app'ingizning ishga tushirish kodi o'sha bundle'lardagi mavjud ishga "
"tushirish kodi bilan ziddiyatga kiradi."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:106
msgid "3. XML view that calls the assets bundle"
msgstr "3. Assets bundle'ni chaqiruvchi XML view"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:108
msgid ""
"Now that we have created our assets bundle, we need to create a :ref:`QWeb "
"view <reference/view_architectures/qweb>` that uses that assets bundle."
msgstr ""
"Assets bundle'ni yaratganimizdan so'ng, endi o'sha assets bundle'dan "
"foydalanadigan :ref:`QWeb view <reference/view_architectures/qweb>` yaratish "
"kerak."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:132
msgid ""
"This template only does two things: it initializes the `odoo` global "
"variable, then calls the assets bundle we just defined. Initializing the "
"`odoo` global variable is a necessary step. This variable should be an "
"object that contains the following:"
msgstr ""
"Bu template faqat ikkita ishni bajaradi: `odoo` global o'zgaruvchisini ishga "
"tayyorlaydi, so'ngra biz hozir aniqlagan assets bundle'ni chaqiradi. `odoo` "
"global o'zgaruvchisini initsializatsiya qilish zaruriy qadam. Bu o'zgaruvchi "
"quyidagilarni o'z ichiga olgan object bo'lishi kerak:"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:136
msgid ""
"The CSRF token, which is required to interact with HTTP controllers in many "
"cases."
msgstr ""
"CSRF token — ko'p hollarda HTTP controller'lar bilan ishlash uchun talab "
"qilinadi."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:137
msgid ""
"The debug value, which is used in many places to add additional logging or "
"developer-friendly checks."
msgstr ""
"Debug qiymati — ko'p joylarda qo'shimcha logging yoki dasturchi uchun qulay "
"tekshiruvlarni qo'shish uchun ishlatiladi."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:138
msgid ""
"`__session_info__`, that contains information from the server that is always "
"needed and for which we don't want to perform an additional request. More on "
"this in the next section."
msgstr ""
"`__session_info__` — serverdan olinadigan, doim kerak bo'ladigan va buning "
"uchun qo'shimcha request bajarishni istamaydigan ma'lumotlarni o'z ichiga "
"oladi. Bu haqda keyingi bo'limda batafsil."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:142
msgid "4. Controller that renders the view"
msgstr "4. View'ni render qiluvchi controller"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:144
msgid ""
"Now that we have the view, we need to make it accessible to the user. For "
"that purpose, we will create an :ref:`HTTP controller<reference/"
"controllers>` that renders that view and returns it to the user."
msgstr ""
"View tayyor bo'lgach, uni foydalanuvchi uchun ochiq qilishimiz kerak. Shu "
"maqsadda o'sha view'ni render qilib, foydalanuvchiga qaytaradigan :ref:`HTTP "
"controller<reference/controllers>` yaratamiz."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:161
msgid ""
"Notice how we're giving the template `session_info`. We get it from the "
"`get_frontend_session_info` method, and it will end up containing "
"information used by the web framework, such as the current user's ID if they "
"are logged in, the server version, the Odoo edition, etc."
msgstr ""
"Template'ga `session_info` ni qanday berayotganimizga e'tibor bering. Uni "
"`get_frontend_session_info` method'idan olamiz va u web framework "
"foydalanadigan ma'lumotlarni o'z ichiga oladi: masalan, tizimga kirgan "
"bo'lsa joriy foydalanuvchining ID'si, server versiyasi, Odoo edition va h.k."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/standalone_owl_application.rst:165
msgid ""
"At this point, if you open the url `/your_module/standalone_app` in your "
"brower, you should see a blank page with the text \"Hello, World!\". At this "
"point, you can start actually writing the code for your app."
msgstr ""
"Shu nuqtada brauzeringizda `/your_module/standalone_app` url'ini ochsangiz, "
"\"Hello, World!\" matni bo'lgan bo'sh sahifani ko'rishingiz kerak. Endi "
"app'ingiz uchun haqiqiy kod yozishni boshlashingiz mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/translations.rst:5
msgid "Translating Modules"
msgstr "Modullarni tarjima qilish"

#: ../../content/developer/howtos/translations.rst:7
msgid ""
"This section explains how to provide translation abilities to your module."
msgstr ""
"Bu bo'limda modulingizga tarjima imkoniyatlarini qanday qo'shish "
