#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/orm.rst:748
msgid "The recommended way to build SQL queries is to use the wrapper object"
msgstr ""
"SQL so'rovlarini tuzishning tavsiya etilgan usuli — wrapper obyektidan "
"foydalanish"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/orm.rst:755
msgid ""
"One important thing to know about models is that they don't necessarily "
"perform database updates right away. Indeed, for performance reasons, the "
"framework delays the recomputation of fields after modifying records. And "
"some database updates are delayed, too. Therefore, before querying the "
"database, one has to make sure that it contains the relevant data for the "
"query. This operation is called *flushing* and performs the expected "
"database updates."
msgstr ""
"Model'lar haqida bilish kerak bo'lgan muhim jihat shundaki, ular ma'lumotlar "
"bazasi yangilanishlarini har doim darhol bajarmaydi. Haqiqatan ham, "
"unumdorlik sabablari uchun framework record'lar o'zgartirilgandan keyin "
"field'larni qayta hisoblashni kechiktiradi. Ba'zi ma'lumotlar bazasi "
"yangilanishlari ham kechiktiriladi. Shu sababli, ma'lumotlar bazasiga so'rov "
"yuborishdan oldin unda so'rov uchun kerakli ma'lumotlar borligiga ishonch "
"hosil qilish kerak. Bu amal *flushing* deb ataladi va kutilgan ma'lumotlar "
"bazasi yangilanishlarini bajaradi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/orm.rst:772
msgid ""
"Before every SQL query, one has to flush the data needed for that query. "
"There are three levels for flushing, each with its own API. One can flush "
"either everything, all the records of a model, or some specific records. "
"Because delaying updates improves performance in general, we recommend to be "
"*specific* when flushing."
msgstr ""
"Har bir SQL so'rovidan oldin shu so'rov uchun kerakli ma'lumotlarni flush "
"qilish kerak. Flush qilishning uchta darajasi bor va har birining o'z API'si "
"mavjud. Hamma narsani, model'ning barcha record'larini yoki ayrim aniq "
"record'larni flush qilish mumkin. Yangilanishlarni kechiktirish umuman "
"unumdorlikni oshirganligi sababli, flush qilishda *aniq* bo'lishni tavsiya "
"qilamiz."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/orm.rst:784
msgid ""
"Because models use the same cursor and the :class:`~odoo.api.Environment` "
"holds various caches, these caches must be invalidated when *altering* the "
"database in raw SQL, or further uses of models may become incoherent. It is "
"necessary to clear caches when using ``CREATE``, ``UPDATE`` or ``DELETE`` in "
"SQL, but not ``SELECT`` (which simply reads the database)."
msgstr ""
"Model'lar bir xil cursor'dan foydalanganligi "
"va :class:`~odoo.api.Environment` turli cache'larni saqlaganligi sababli, "
"xom SQL bilan ma'lumotlar bazasini *o'zgartirganda* bu cache'lar invalidate "
"qilinishi kerak, aks holda model'lardan keyingi foydalanish nomuvofiq bo'lib "
"qolishi mumkin. SQL'da ``CREATE``, ``UPDATE`` yoki ``DELETE`` ishlatilganda "
"cache'ni tozalash zarur, lekin ``SELECT`` uchun kerak emas (u shunchaki "
"ma'lumotlar bazasini o'qiydi)."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/orm.rst:802
msgid ""
"Just like flushing, one can invalidate either the whole cache, the cache of "
"all the records of a model, or the cache of specific records. One can even "
"invalidate specific fields on some records or all records of a model. As the "
"cache improves performance in general, we recommend to be *specific* when "
"invalidating."
msgstr ""
"Flush qilish kabi, butun cache'ni, model'ning barcha record'lari cache'ini "
"yoki aniq record'lar cache'ini invalidate qilish mumkin. Hatto ayrim "
"record'lardagi yoki model'ning barcha record'laridagi aniq field'larni ham "
"invalidate qilish mumkin. Cache umuman unumdorlikni oshirganligi sababli, "
"invalidate qilishda *aniq* bo'lishni tavsiya qilamiz."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/orm.rst:814
msgid ""
"The methods above keep the caches and the database consistent with each "
"other. However, if computed field dependencies have been modified in the "
"database, one has to inform the models for the computed fields to be "
"recomputed. The only thing the framework needs to know is *what* fields have "
"changed on *which* records."
msgstr ""
"Yuqoridagi method'lar cache'lar va ma'lumotlar bazasini bir-biriga muvofiq "
"holda saqlaydi. Biroq, agar computed field bog'liqliklari ma'lumotlar "
"bazasida o'zgartirilgan bo'lsa, computed field'lar qayta hisoblanishi uchun "
"model'larni xabardor qilish kerak. Framework bilishi kerak bo'lgan yagona "
"narsa — *qaysi* record'larda *qanday* field'lar o'zgargani."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/orm.rst:836
msgid ""
"One has to figure out which records have been modified. There are many ways "
"to do this, possibly involving extra SQL queries. In the example above, we "
"take advantage of the ``RETURNING`` clause of PostgreSQL to retrieve the "
"information without an extra query. After making the cache consistent by "
"invalidation, invoke the method ``modified`` on the modified records with "
"the fields that have been updated."
msgstr ""
"Qaysi record'lar o'zgartirilganini aniqlash kerak. Buni amalga oshirishning "
"ko'p usullari bor, ehtimol qo'shimcha SQL so'rovlarini talab qiladi. "
"Yuqoridagi misolda ma'lumotni qo'shimcha so'rovsiz olish uchun "
"PostgreSQL'ning ``RETURNING`` bandidan foydalanamiz. Cache'ni invalidate "
"qilish orqali muvofiq holga keltirgandan so'ng, o'zgartirilgan record'larda "
"yangilangan field'lar bilan ``modified`` method'ini chaqiring."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/orm.rst:849
msgid "Common ORM methods"
msgstr "Keng tarqalgan ORM method'lari"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/orm.rst:854
