"By default, the profiler enables the SQL and the Periodic collectors. Both "
"when it is enabled from the user interface or Python code."
msgstr ""
"Standart holatda profiler SQL va Periodic collector'larni yoqadi. Bu "
"foydalanuvchi interfeysidan yoki Python kodidan yoqilganda ham amal qiladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:210
msgid "SQL collector"
msgstr "SQL collector"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:212
msgid ""
"The SQL collector saves all the SQL queries made to the database in the "
"current thread (for all cursors), as well as the stack trace. The overhead "
"of the collector is added to the analysed thread for each query, which means "
"that using it on a lot of small queries may impact execution time and other "
"profilers."
msgstr ""
"SQL collector joriy thread'da ma'lumotlar bazasiga yuborilgan barcha SQL "
"so'rovlarini (barcha cursor'lar uchun) va stack trace'ni saqlaydi. "
"Collector'ning qo'shimcha xarajati har bir so'rov uchun tahlil qilinayotgan "
"thread'ga qo'shiladi, ya'ni uni ko'p mayda so'rovlarda ishlatish bajarilish "
"vaqtiga va boshqa profiler'larga ta'sir qilishi mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:217
msgid ""
"It is especially useful to debug query counts, or to add information to "
"the :ref:`Periodic collector <performance/profiling/collectors/periodic>` in "
"the combined speedscope view."
msgstr ""
"U so'rovlar sonini debug qilish, yoki combined speedscope "
"ko'rinishida :ref:`Periodic collector <performance/profiling/collectors/"
"periodic>` ma'lumotlarini to'ldirish uchun ayniqsa foydali."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:225
msgid "Periodic collector"
msgstr "Periodic collector"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:227
msgid ""
"This collector runs in a separate thread and saves the stack trace of the "
"analysed thread at every interval. The interval (by default 10 ms) can be "
"defined through the :guilabel:`Interval` option in the user interface, or "
"the `interval` parameter in Python code."
msgstr ""
"Bu collector alohida thread'da ishlaydi va tahlil qilinayotgan thread'ning "
"stack trace'ini har bir interval'da saqlaydi. Interval (standart holatda 10 "
"ms) foydalanuvchi interfeysidagi :guilabel:`Interval` parametri orqali, yoki "
"Python kodidagi `interval` parametri orqali aniqlanadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:232
msgid ""
"If the interval is set at a very low value, profiling long requests will "
"generate memory issues. If the interval is set at a very high value, "
"information on short function executions will be lost."
msgstr ""
"Agar interval juda kichik qiymatga qo'yilsa, uzun request'larni profiling "
"qilish xotira muammolarini keltirib chiqaradi. Agar interval juda katta "
"qiymatga qo'yilsa, qisqa funksiya bajarilishlari haqidagi ma'lumot yo'qoladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:236
msgid ""
"It is one of the best way to analyse performance as it should have a very "
"low impact on the execution time thanks to its separate thread."
msgstr ""
"Alohida thread'da ishlagani uchun bajarilish vaqtiga juda kam ta'sir qiladi, "
"shu sababli u unumdorlikni tahlil qilishning eng yaxshi usullaridan biridir."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:244
msgid "QWeb collector"
msgstr "QWeb collector"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:246
msgid ""
"This collector saves the Python execution time and queries of all "
"directives. As for the :ref:`SQL collector <performance/profiling/collectors/"
"sql>`, the overhead can be important when executing a lot of small "
"directives. The results are different from other collectors in terms of "
"collected data, and can be analysed from the `ir.profile` form view using a "
"custom widget."
msgstr ""
"Bu collector barcha directive'larning Python bajarilish vaqti va "
"so'rovlarini saqlaydi. :ref:`SQL collector <performance/profiling/collectors/"
"sql>` singari, ko'p mayda directive'lar bajarilganda qo'shimcha xarajat "
"sezilarli bo'lishi mumkin. Natijalar yig'ilgan ma'lumot jihatidan boshqa "
"collector'lardan farq qiladi va ularni `ir.profile` form view'idan maxsus "
"widget yordamida tahlil qilish mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:251
msgid "It is mainly useful for optimizing views."
msgstr "U asosan view'larni optimallashtirish uchun foydali."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:258
msgid "Sync collector"
msgstr "Sync collector"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:260
msgid ""
"This collector saves the stack for every function's call and return and runs "
"on the same thread, which greatly impacts performance."
msgstr ""
"Bu collector har bir funksiya chaqirilishi va qaytishi uchun stack'ni "
"saqlaydi hamda o'sha thread'da ishlaydi, bu esa unumdorlikka kuchli ta'sir "
"qiladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:263
msgid ""
"It can be useful to debug and understand complex flows, and follow their "
"execution in the code. It is however not recommended for performance "
"analysis because the overhead is high."
msgstr ""
"U murakkab oqimlarni debug qilish va tushunish, hamda ularning kodda "
"bajarilishini kuzatish uchun foydali bo'lishi mumkin. Biroq qo'shimcha "
"xarajat yuqori bo'lgani uchun unumdorlik tahlili uchun tavsiya etilmaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:271
msgid "Performance pitfalls"
msgstr "Unumdorlikdagi tuzoqlar"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:273
msgid ""
"Be careful with randomness. Multiple executions may lead to different "
"results. E.g., a garbage collector being triggered during execution."
msgstr ""
"Tasodifiylikka ehtiyot bo'ling. Bir necha marta bajarish turli natijalarga "
"olib kelishi mumkin. Masalan, bajarilish vaqtida garbage collector ishga "
"tushishi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:275
msgid ""
"Be careful with blocking calls. In some cases, external `c_call` may take "
"some time before releasing the GIL, thus leading to unexpected long frames "
"with the :ref:`Periodic collector <performance/profiling/collectors/"
"periodic>`. This should be detected by the profiler and give a warning. It "
"is possible to trigger the profiler manually before such calls if needed."
msgstr ""
"Bloklovchi chaqiruvlarga ehtiyot bo'ling. Ba'zi hollarda tashqi `c_call` "
"GIL'ni bo'shatishdan oldin biroz vaqt olishi mumkin, bu esa :ref:`Periodic "
"collector <performance/profiling/collectors/periodic>` bilan kutilmagan uzun "
"frame'larga olib keladi. Buni profiler aniqlashi va ogohlantirish berishi "
"kerak. Zarur bo'lsa, bunday chaqiruvlardan oldin profiler'ni qo'lda ishga "
"tushirish mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:279
msgid ""
"Pay attention to the cache. Profiling before that the `view`/`assets`/... "
"are in cache can lead to different results."
msgstr ""
"Cache'ga e'tibor bering. `view`/`assets`/... cache'ga tushishidan oldin "
"profiling qilish turli natijalarga olib kelishi mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:281
msgid ""
"Be aware of the profiler's overhead. The :ref:`SQL collector <performance/"
"profiling/collectors/sql>`'s overhead can be important when a lot of small "
"queries are executed. Profiling is practical to spot a problem but you may "
"want to disable the profiler in order to measure the real impact of a code "
"change."
msgstr ""
"Profiler'ning qo'shimcha xarajatini yodda tuting. Ko'p mayda so'rovlar "
"bajarilganda :ref:`SQL collector <performance/profiling/collectors/"
"sql>`'ning qo'shimcha xarajati sezilarli bo'lishi mumkin. Profiling muammoni "
"topish uchun qulay, biroq kod o'zgarishining haqiqiy ta'sirini o'lchash "
"uchun profiler'ni o'chirib qo'yish kerak bo'lishi mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:285
msgid ""
"Profiling results can be memory intensive. In some cases (e.g., profiling an "
"install or a long request), it is possible that you reach memory limit, "
"especially when rendering the speedscope results, which can lead to an HTTP "
"500 error. In this case, you may need to start the server with a higher "
"memory limit: `--limit-memory-hard $((8*1024**3))`."
msgstr ""
"Profiling natijalari ko'p xotira talab qilishi mumkin. Ba'zi hollarda "
"(masalan, install yoki uzun request'ni profiling qilishda) xotira "
"chegarasiga yetib qolishingiz mumkin, ayniqsa speedscope natijalarini render "
"qilganda, bu esa HTTP 500 xatosiga olib kelishi mumkin. Bunday holatda "
"serverni yuqoriroq xotira chegarasi bilan ishga tushirish kerak bo'lishi "
"mumkin: `--limit-memory-hard $((8*1024**3))`."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:293
msgid "Good practices"
msgstr "Yaxshi amaliyotlar"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:298
msgid "Batch operations"
msgstr "Batch operatsiyalar"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:300
msgid ""
"When working with recordsets, it is almost always better to batch operations."
msgstr ""
"Recordset'lar bilan ishlaganda operatsiyalarni batch qilish deyarli har doim "
"yaxshiroq."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:303
msgid ""
"Don't call a method that runs SQL queries while looping over a recordset "
"because it will do so for each record of the set."
msgstr ""
"Recordset bo'ylab loop qilayotganda SQL so'rovlarini bajaradigan method'ni "
"chaqirmang, chunki u to'plamdagi har bir record uchun shunday qiladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:314
msgid ""
"Instead, replace the `search_count` with a `_read_group` to execute one SQL "
"query for the entire batch of records."
msgstr ""
"Buning o'rniga, record'larning butun batch'i uchun bitta SQL so'rovi "
"bajarilishi maqsadida `search_count` ni `_read_group` bilan almashtiring."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:328
msgid ""
"This example is not optimal nor correct in all cases. It is only a "
"substitute for a `search_count`. Another solution could be to prefetch and "
"count the inverse `One2many` field."
msgstr ""
"Bu misol barcha holatlarda optimal ham, to'g'ri ham emas. U faqat "
"`search_count` o'rnini bosuvchi variant. Boshqa yechim — teskari `One2many` "
"field'ini prefetch qilib, sanash bo'lishi mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:332
msgid "Don't create records one after another."
msgstr "Record'larni birin-ketin yaratmang."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:340
msgid ""
"Instead, accumulate the create values and call the `create` method on the "
"batch. Doing so has mostly no impact and helps the framework optimize fields "
"computation."
msgstr ""
"Buning o'rniga, create qiymatlarini to'plang va batch ustida `create` "
"method'ini chaqiring. Bunday qilish ko'p hollarda hech qanday ta'sir "
"ko'rsatmaydi va framework'ga field'lar hisoblanishini optimallashtirishga "
"yordam beradi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:352
msgid ""
"Fail to prefetch the fields of a recordset while browsing a single record "
"inside a loop."
msgstr ""
"Loop ichida bitta record'ni browse qilganda recordset field'lari prefetch "
"qilinmaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:361
msgid "Instead, browse the entire recordset first."
msgstr "Buning o'rniga, avval butun recordset'ni browse qiling."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:370
msgid ""
"We can verify that the records are prefetched in batch by reading the field "
"`prefetch_ids` which includes each of the record ids.browsing all records "
"together is unpractical,"
msgstr ""
"`prefetch_ids` field'ini o'qib, record'lar batch tarzida prefetch "
"qilinganini tekshirishimiz mumkin — u har bir record id'sini o'z ichiga "
"oladi. Barcha record'larni birgalikda browse qilish amaliy emas,"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:373
msgid ""
"If needed, the `with_prefetch` method can be used to disable batch "
"prefetching:"
msgstr ""
"Agar kerak bo'lsa, batch prefetching'ni o'chirish uchun `with_prefetch` "
"method'idan foydalanish mumkin:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:383
msgid "Reduce the algorithmic complexity"
msgstr "Algoritmik murakkablikni kamaytirish"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:385
msgid ""
"Algorithmic complexity is a measure of how long an algorithm would take to "
"complete in regard to the size `n` of the input. When the complexity is "
"high, the execution time can grow quickly as the input becomes larger. In "
"some cases, the algorithmic complexity can be reduced by preparing the "
"input's data correctly."
msgstr ""
"Algoritmik murakkablik — algoritmning kirish ma'lumotlari hajmi `n` ga "
"nisbatan qancha vaqtda bajarilishini o'lchaydigan ko'rsatkich. Murakkablik "
"yuqori bo'lganda, kirish hajmi kattalashgani sari bajarilish vaqti tez o'sib "
"ketadi. Ba'zi hollarda kirish ma'lumotlarini to'g'ri tayyorlash orqali "
"algoritmik murakkablikni kamaytirish mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:391
msgid ""
"For a given problem, let's consider a naive algorithm crafted with two "
"nested loops for which the complexity in in O(n²)."
msgstr ""
"Berilgan masala uchun ikkita ichma-ich loop bilan yozilgan sodda algoritmni "
"ko'rib chiqaylik — uning murakkabligi O(n²)."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:403
msgid ""
"Assuming that all results have a different id, we can prepare the data to "
"reduce the complexity."
msgstr ""
"Barcha natijalar turli id'ga ega deb hisoblasak, murakkablikni kamaytirish "
"uchun ma'lumotlarni tayyorlashimiz mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:413
msgid ""
"Choosing the bad data structure to hold the input can lead to quadratic "
"complexity."
msgstr ""
"Kirish ma'lumotlarini saqlash uchun noto'g'ri ma'lumot strukturasini tanlash "
"kvadratik murakkablikka olib kelishi mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:423
msgid ""
"If `invalid_ids` is a list-like data structure, the complexity of the "
"algorithm may be quadratic."
msgstr ""
"Agar `invalid_ids` list'ga o'xshash ma'lumot strukturasi bo'lsa, "
"algoritmning murakkabligi kvadratik bo'lishi mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:425
msgid ""
"Instead, prefer using set operations like casting `invalid_ids` to a set."
msgstr ""
"Buning o'rniga set amallaridan foydalanishni afzal ko'ring, masalan "
"`invalid_ids` ni set'ga o'tkazing."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:435
msgid "Depending on the input, recordset operations can also be used."
msgstr ""
"Kirish ma'lumotlariga qarab recordset amallaridan ham foydalanish mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:447
msgid "Use indexes"
msgstr "Index'lardan foydalanish"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:449
msgid ""
"Database indexes can help fasten search operations, be it from a search in "
"the or through the user interface."
msgstr ""
"Ma'lumotlar bazasi index'lari qidiruv amallarini tezlashtirishga yordam "
"beradi — qidiruv kodda yoki foydalanuvchi interfeysi orqali bajarilishidan "
"qat'i nazar."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/performance.rst:457
msgid ""
"Be careful not to index every field as indexes consume space and impact on "
"performance when executing one of `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, and `DELETE`."
msgstr ""
"Har bir field'ni index'lamaslikka e'tibor bering, chunki index'lar joy "
"egallaydi va `INSERT`, `UPDATE` hamda `DELETE` amallaridan birini bajarishda "
"unumdorlikka ta'sir qiladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/reports.rst:10
msgid "QWeb Reports"
msgstr "QWeb report'lar"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/reports.rst:12
msgid ""
"Reports are written in HTML/QWeb, like website views in Odoo. You can use "
"the usual :ref:`QWeb control flow tools <reference/qweb>`. The PDF rendering "
"itself is performed by wkhtmltopdf_."
msgstr ""
"Report'lar Odoo'dagi website view'lari kabi HTML/QWeb'da yoziladi. Siz "
"odatdagi :ref:`QWeb control flow vositalaridan <reference/qweb>` "
"foydalanishingiz mumkin. PDF rendering'ning o'zi wkhtmltopdf_ tomonidan "
"bajariladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/reports.rst:16
msgid ""
"Reports are declared using a :ref:`report action <reference/actions/"
"report>`, and a :ref:`reference/reports/templates` for the action to use."
msgstr ""
"Report'lar :ref:`report action <reference/actions/report>` yordamida e'lon "
"qilinadi, shuningdek action foydalanishi uchun :ref:`reference/reports/"
"templates` kerak bo'ladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/reports.rst:19
msgid ""
"If useful or necessary, it is possible to specify a :ref:`reference/reports/"
"paper_formats` for the report report."
msgstr ""
"Agar foydali yoki zarur bo'lsa, report uchun :ref:`reference/reports/"
"paper_formats` ni belgilash mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/reports.rst:25
msgid "Report template"
msgstr "Report template"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/reports.rst:27
