#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:6
msgid "Security in Odoo"
msgstr "Odoo'da xavfsizlik"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:8
msgid ""
"Aside from manually managing access using custom code, Odoo provides two "
"main data-driven mechanisms to manage or restrict access to data."
msgstr ""
"Maxsus kod yordamida kirish huquqlarini qo'lda boshqarishdan tashqari, Odoo "
"ma'lumotlarga kirishni boshqarish yoki cheklash uchun ma'lumotlarga "
"asoslangan ikkita asosiy mexanizmni taqdim etadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:11
msgid ""
"Both mechanisms are linked to specific users through *groups*: a user "
"belongs to any number of groups, and security mechanisms are associated to "
"groups, thus applying security mechanisms to users."
msgstr ""
"Ikkala mexanizm ham *group'lar* orqali muayyan foydalanuvchilarga "
"bog'lanadi: foydalanuvchi istalgan sondagi group'larga tegishli bo'lishi "
"mumkin, xavfsizlik mexanizmlari esa group'larga bog'lanadi va shu yo'l bilan "
"foydalanuvchilarga qo'llaniladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:19
msgid ""
"serves as user-readable identification for the group (spells out the role / "
"purpose of the group)"
msgstr ""
"group uchun foydalanuvchi o'qiy oladigan identifikator sifatida xizmat "
"qiladi (group'ning roli / maqsadini ifodalaydi)"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:24
msgid ""
"The *module category*, serves to associate groups with an Odoo App (~a set "
"of related business models) and convert them into an exclusive selection in "
"the user form."
msgstr ""
"*module category* group'larni Odoo App (~o'zaro bog'liq business model'lar "
"to'plami) bilan bog'lash va ularni foydalanuvchi form'ida yagona tanlovga "
"aylantirish uchun xizmat qiladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:28
msgid ""
"clarify & document special cases & relationship between groups & categories "
"better"
msgstr ""
"maxsus holatlarni hamda group'lar va category'lar orasidagi munosabatni "
"yaxshiroq aniqlashtirish va hujjatlashtirish"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:33
msgid ""
"Other groups to set on the user alongside this one. This is a convenience "
"pseudo-inheritance relationship: it's possible to explicitly remove implied "
"groups from a user without removing the implier."
msgstr ""
"Foydalanuvchiga bu group bilan birga o'rnatiladigan boshqa group'lar. Bu "
"qulaylik uchun mo'ljallangan psevdo-inheritance munosabati: nazarda tutilgan "
"group'larni ularni nazarda tutuvchi group'ni olib tashlamasdan "
"foydalanuvchidan aniq ravishda olib tashlash mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:40
msgid "Additional notes on the group e.g."
msgstr "Group haqida qo'shimcha izohlar, masalan"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:45
#: ../../content/developer/reference/external_api.rst:386
#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/restrict_data_access.rst:133
#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/server_framework_101/04_securityintro.rst:67
msgid "Access Rights"
msgstr "Kirish huquqlari"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:47
msgid ""
"*Grants* access to an entire model for a given set of operations. If no "
"access rights matches an operation on a model for a user (through their "
"group), the user doesn't have access."
msgstr ""
"Berilgan operatsiyalar to'plami uchun butun model'ga kirishni *beradi*. Agar "
"foydalanuvchi uchun (uning group'i orqali) model'dagi operatsiyaga mos "
"keladigan kirish huquqi bo'lmasa, foydalanuvchi kirish huquqiga ega "
"bo'lmaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:51
msgid ""
"Access rights are additive, a user's accesses are the union of the accesses "
"they get through all their groups e.g. given a user who is part of group A "
"granting read and create access and a group B granting update access, the "
"user will have all three of create, read, and update."
msgstr ""
"Kirish huquqlari qo'shiluvchi hisoblanadi: foydalanuvchining kirish "
"huquqlari uning barcha group'lari orqali oladigan huquqlar birlashmasidir. "
"Masalan, foydalanuvchi read va create huquqini beruvchi A group'ining va "
"update huquqini beruvchi B group'ining a'zosi bo'lsa, u create, read va "
"update - uchchalasiga ham ega bo'ladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:60
msgid "The purpose or role of the group."
msgstr "Group'ning maqsadi yoki roli."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:64
msgid "The model whose access the ACL controls."
msgstr "ACL kirishini nazorat qiladigan model."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:68
msgid ""
"The :class:`res.groups` to which the accesses are granted, an "
"empty :attr:`group_id` means the ACL is granted to *every user* (non-"
"employees e.g. portal or public users)."
msgstr ""
"Kirish huquqlari beriladigan :class:`res.groups`; bo'sh :attr:`group_id` ACL "
"*har bir foydalanuvchiga* berilganini bildiradi (xodim bo'lmaganlar, masalan "
"portal yoki public foydalanuvchilar)."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:72
msgid ""
"The :samp:`perm_{method}` attributes grant the corresponding CRUD access "
"when set, they are all unset by default."
msgstr ""
":samp:`perm_{method}` attribute'lari o'rnatilganda mos keluvchi CRUD "
"kirishini beradi; standart holatda ularning barchasi o'rnatilmagan."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:83
#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/restrict_data_access.rst:198
msgid "Record Rules"
msgstr "Record rule'lar"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:85
msgid ""
"Record rules are *conditions* which must be satisfied in order for an "
"operation to be allowed. Record rules are evaluated record-by-record, "
"following access rights."
msgstr ""
"Record rule'lar - operatsiyaga ruxsat berilishi uchun bajarilishi shart "
"bo'lgan *shartlar*. Record rule'lar kirish huquqlaridan keyin har bir record "
"uchun alohida baholanadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:89
msgid ""
"Record rules are default-allow: if access rights grant access and no rule "
"applies to the operation and model for the user, the access is granted."
msgstr ""
"Record rule'lar standart holatda ruxsat beruvchi: agar kirish huquqlari "
"ruxsat bergan bo'lsa va foydalanuvchi uchun ushbu operatsiya va model'ga "
"hech qanday rule qo'llanilmasa, kirishga ruxsat beriladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:96
msgid "The description of the rule."
msgstr "Rule'ning ta'rifi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:100
msgid "The model to which the rule applies."
msgstr "Rule qo'llaniladigan model."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:104
msgid ""
"The :class:`res.groups` to which access is granted (or not). Multiple groups "
"can be specified. If no group is specified, the rule is *global* which is "
"treated differently than \"group\" rules (see below)."
msgstr ""
"Kirish beriladigan (yoki berilmaydigan) :class:`res.groups`. Bir nechta "
"group ko'rsatilishi mumkin. Agar hech qanday group ko'rsatilmasa, rule "
"*global* bo'ladi va u \"group\" rule'laridan farqli tarzda ishlanadi (quyida "
"ko'ring)."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:110
msgid ""
"Computed on the basis of :attr:`groups`, provides easy access to the global "
"status (or not) of the rule."
msgstr ""
":attr:`groups` asosida hisoblanadi va rule'ning global holati (yoki "
"emasligi) haqidagi ma'lumotni oson olish imkonini beradi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:115
msgid ""
"A predicate specified as a :ref:`domain <reference/orm/domains>`, the rule "
"allows the selected operations if the domain matches the record, and forbids "
"it otherwise."
msgstr ""
":ref:`domain <reference/orm/domains>` sifatida ko'rsatilgan predikat; agar "
"domain record'ga mos kelsa, rule tanlangan operatsiyalarga ruxsat beradi, "
"aks holda taqiqlaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:119
msgid ""
"The domain is a *python expression* which can use the following variables:"
msgstr ""
"Domain - quyidagi o'zgaruvchilardan foydalanishi mumkin bo'lgan *python "
"expression*:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:123
msgid "Python's :mod:`python:time` module."
msgstr "Python'ning :mod:`python:time` module'i."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:125
msgid "The current user, as a singleton recordset."
msgstr "Joriy foydalanuvchi, singleton recordset sifatida."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:127
msgid "``company_id``"
msgstr "``company_id``"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:127
msgid ""
"The current user's currently selected company as a single company id (not a "
"recordset)."
msgstr ""
"Joriy foydalanuvchi tanlab qo'ygan company, yagona company id sifatida "
"(recordset emas)."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:131
msgid "``company_ids``"
msgstr "``company_ids``"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:130
msgid ""
"All the companies to which the current user has access as a list of company "
"ids (not a recordset), see :ref:`howto/company/security` for more details."
msgstr ""
"Joriy foydalanuvchi kirish huquqiga ega bo'lgan barcha company'lar, company "
"id'lar ro'yxati sifatida (recordset emas); batafsil ma'lumot "
"uchun :ref:`howto/company/security` ga qarang."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:134
msgid ""
"The :samp:`perm_{method}` have completely different semantics than "
"for :class:`ir.model.access`: for rules, they specify which operation the "
"rules applies *for*. If an operation is not selected, then the rule is not "
"checked for it, as if the rule did not exist."
msgstr ""
":samp:`perm_{method}` field'lari :class:`ir.model.access` dagidan butunlay "
"boshqa semantikaga ega: rule'lar uchun ular rule qaysi operatsiya *uchun* "
"qo'llanilishini ko'rsatadi. Agar operatsiya tanlanmagan bo'lsa, rule u uchun "
"tekshirilmaydi — go'yo rule mavjud emas."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:139
msgid "All operations are selected by default."
msgstr "Sukut bo'yicha barcha operatsiyalar tanlangan."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:149
msgid "Global rules versus group rules"
msgstr "Global rule'lar va group rule'lar"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:151
msgid ""
"There is a large difference between global and group rules in how they "
"compose and combine:"
msgstr ""
"Global va group rule'lar o'zaro qanday qo'shilishi va birlashishida katta "
"farq bor:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:154
msgid ""
"Global rules *intersect*, if two global rules apply then *both* must be "
"satisfied for the access to be granted, this means adding global rules "
"always restricts access further."
msgstr ""
"Global rule'lar *kesishadi*: agar ikkita global rule qo'llanilsa, kirish "
"berilishi uchun *ikkisi ham* bajarilishi shart; ya'ni global rule qo'shish "
"har doim kirishni yanada cheklaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:157
msgid ""
"Group rules *unify*, if two group rules apply then *either* can be satisfied "
"for the access to be granted. This means adding group rules can expand "
"access, but not beyond the bounds defined by global rules."
msgstr ""
"Group rule'lar *birlashadi*: agar ikkita group rule qo'llanilsa, kirish "
"berilishi uchun *ulardan biri* bajarilishi kifoya. Ya'ni group rule qo'shish "
"kirishni kengaytirishi mumkin, lekin global rule'lar belgilagan chegaradan "
"tashqariga chiqmaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:160
msgid ""
"The global and group rulesets *intersect*, which means the first group rule "
"being added to a given global ruleset will restrict access."
msgstr ""
"Global va group ruleset'lari *kesishadi*, ya'ni mavjud global ruleset'ga "
"qo'shilgan birinchi group rule kirishni cheklaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:165
msgid ""
"Creating multiple global rules is risky as it's possible to create non-"
"overlapping rulesets, which will remove all access."
msgstr ""
"Bir nechta global rule yaratish xatarli, chunki bir-biri bilan "
"kesishmaydigan ruleset'lar hosil bo'lishi mumkin va bu barcha kirishni yo'q "
"qiladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:171
msgid "Field Access"
msgstr "Field'ga kirish"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:173
msgid ""
"An ORM :class:`~odoo.fields.Field` can have a ``groups`` attribute providing "
"a list of groups (as a comma-separated string of :term:`external "
"identifiers`)."
msgstr ""
"ORM :class:`~odoo.fields.Field` ``groups`` atributiga ega bo'lishi mumkin — "
"u group'lar ro'yxatini beradi (vergul bilan ajratilgan :term:`external "
"identifiers` satri sifatida)."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:177
msgid ""
"If the current user is not in one of the listed groups, he will not have "
"access to the field:"
msgstr ""
"Agar joriy foydalanuvchi sanab o'tilgan group'lardan birida bo'lmasa, u "
"field'ga kirish huquqiga ega bo'lmaydi:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:180
msgid "restricted fields are automatically removed from requested views"
msgstr "cheklangan field'lar so'ralgan view'lardan avtomatik olib tashlanadi"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:181
msgid ""
"restricted fields are removed from :meth:`~odoo.models.Model.fields_get` "
"responses"
msgstr ""
"cheklangan field'lar :meth:`~odoo.models.Model.fields_get` javoblaridan olib "
"tashlanadi"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:183
msgid ""
"attempts to (explicitly) read from or write to restricted fields results in "
"an access error"
msgstr ""
"cheklangan field'lardan (ochiq-oydin) o'qish yoki ularga yozish urinishlari "
"kirish xatosiga olib keladi"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:188
msgid ""
"field access groups apply to the Superuser in fields_get but not in read/"
"write..."
msgstr ""
"field access group'lari fields_get da Superuser'ga ham qo'llanadi, lekin "
"read/write da qo'llanmaydi..."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:197
msgid "Security Pitfalls"
msgstr "Xavfsizlikdagi tipik xatolar"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:199
msgid ""
"As a developer, it is important to understand the security mechanisms and "
"avoid common mistakes leading to insecure code."
msgstr ""
"Dasturchi sifatida xavfsizlik mexanizmlarini tushunish va xavfsiz bo'lmagan "
"kodga olib keladigan keng tarqalgan xatolardan qochish muhim."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:203
msgid "Unsafe Public Methods"
msgstr "Xavfsiz bo'lmagan public method'lar"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:205
msgid ""
"Any public method can be executed via a :ref:`RPC call <api/external_api/"
"calling_methods>` with the chosen parameters. The methods starting with a "
"``_`` are not callable from an action button or external API."
msgstr ""
"Har qanday public method tanlangan parametrlar bilan :ref:`RPC call <api/"
"external_api/calling_methods>` orqali bajarilishi mumkin. ``_`` bilan "
"boshlanadigan method'larni action button yoki external API'dan chaqirib "
"bo'lmaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:209
msgid ""
"On public methods, the record on which a method is executed and the "
"parameters can not be trusted, ACL being only verified during CRUD "
"operations."
msgstr ""
"Public method'larda method bajarilayotgan record ham, parametrlar ham "
"ishonchli deb hisoblanmaydi, chunki ACL faqat CRUD operatsiyalari vaqtida "
"tekshiriladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:223
msgid ""
"Making a method private is obviously not enough and care must be taken to "
"use it properly."
msgstr ""
"Method'ni private qilish, tabiiyki, yetarli emas — uni to'g'ri ishlatishga "
"alohida e'tibor berish kerak."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:227
msgid "Bypassing the ORM"
msgstr "ORM'ni chetlab o'tish"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:229
msgid ""
"You should never use the database cursor directly when the ORM can do the "
"same thing! By doing so you are bypassing all the ORM features, possibly the "
"automated behaviours like translations, invalidation of fields, ``active``, "
"access rights and so on."
msgstr ""
"ORM xuddi shu ishni bajara oladigan holatda ma'lumotlar bazasi cursor'idan "
"bevosita foydalanmang! Bunday qilib siz barcha ORM imkoniyatlarini chetlab "
"o'tasiz — tarjimalar, field'lar invalidatsiyasi, ``active``, kirish "
"huquqlari va shu kabi avtomatik xatti-harakatlarni."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:234
msgid ""
"And chances are that you are also making the code harder to read and "
"probably less secure."
msgstr ""
"Bundan tashqari, siz kodni o'qishni qiyinlashtirasiz va, ehtimol, uni kamroq "
"xavfsiz qilasiz."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:259
msgid "SQL injections"
msgstr "SQL injeksiyalar"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:261
msgid ""
"Care must be taken not to introduce SQL injections vulnerabilities when "
"using manual SQL queries. The vulnerability is present when user input is "
"either incorrectly filtered or badly quoted, allowing an attacker to "
"introduce undesirable clauses to a SQL query (such as circumventing filters "
"or executing ``UPDATE`` or ``DELETE`` commands)."
msgstr ""
"Qo'lda yozilgan SQL so'rovlardan foydalanganda SQL injeksiya zaifliklarini "
"kiritmaslikka e'tibor berish kerak. Zaiflik foydalanuvchi kiritgan ma'lumot "
"noto'g'ri filtrlanganda yoki xato tarzda qo'shtirnoqqa olinganda paydo "
"bo'ladi va hujumchiga SQL so'rovga nomaqbul shartlar qo'shish imkonini "
"beradi (masalan, filtrlarni chetlab o'tish yoki ``UPDATE`` va ``DELETE`` "
"buyruqlarini bajarish)."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:267
msgid ""
"The best way to be safe is to never, NEVER use Python string concatenation "
"(+) or string parameters interpolation (%) to pass variables to a SQL query "
"string."
msgstr ""
"Xavfsiz bo'lishning eng yaxshi usuli — SQL so'rov satriga o'zgaruvchilarni "
"uzatish uchun Python satr birlashtirishdan (+) yoki satr parametrlari "
"interpolatsiyasidan (%) hech qachon, HECH QACHON foydalanmaslikdir."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:270
msgid ""
"The second reason, which is almost as important, is that it is the job of "
"the database abstraction layer (psycopg2) to decide how to format query "
"parameters, not your job! For example psycopg2 knows that when you pass a "
"list of values it needs to format them as a comma-separated list, enclosed "
"in parentheses !"
msgstr ""
"Deyarli shunchalik muhim ikkinchi sabab: so'rov parametrlarini qanday "
"formatlashni hal qilish — ma'lumotlar bazasi abstraksiya qatlamining "
"(psycopg2) vazifasi, sizning emas! Masalan, psycopg2 biladi: siz qiymatlar "
"ro'yxatini uzatganingizda ularni qavs ichiga olingan, vergul bilan "
"ajratilgan ro'yxat shaklida formatlash kerak!"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:275
msgid ""
"Even better, there exists a :class:`~odoo.tools.SQL` wrapper to build "
"queries using templates that handles the formatting of inputs. "
"Check :ref:`SQL execution <reference/orm/sql>` for detailed usage."
msgstr ""
"Bundan ham yaxshisi: kirish qiymatlarini formatlashni o'zi hal qiladigan, "
"template'lar yordamida so'rov qurish uchun :class:`~odoo.tools.SQL` "
"wrapper'i mavjud. Batafsil ishlatilishi uchun :ref:`SQL execution <reference/"
"orm/sql>` bo'limini ko'ring."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:301
msgid ""
"This is very important, so please be careful also when refactoring, and most "
"importantly do not copy these patterns!"
msgstr ""
"Bu juda muhim, shuning uchun refactoring vaqtida ham ehtiyot bo'ling va eng "
"muhimi — bu pattern'larni ko'chirib olmang!"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:304
msgid ""
"Here is a memorable example to help you remember what the issue is about "
"(but do not copy the code there). Before continuing, please be sure to read "
"the online documentation of pyscopg2 to learn of to use it properly:"
msgstr ""
"Muammo nimada ekanini eslab qolishga yordam beradigan yorqin misol (lekin u "
"yerdagi kodni ko'chirib olmang). Davom etishdan oldin psycopg2 ni to'g'ri "
"ishlatishni o'rganish uchun uning onlayn hujjatlarini o'qib chiqing:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:308
msgid ""
"`The problem with query parameters <http://initd.org/psycopg/docs/"
"usage.html#the-problem-with-the-query-parameters>`_"
msgstr ""
"`So'rov parametrlari bilan bog'liq muammo <http://initd.org/psycopg/docs/"
"usage.html#the-problem-with-the-query-parameters>`_"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:309
msgid ""
"`How to pass parameters with psycopg2 <http://initd.org/psycopg/docs/"
"usage.html#passing-parameters-to-sql-queries>`_"
msgstr ""
"`psycopg2 bilan parametrlarni qanday uzatish kerak <http://initd.org/psycopg/"
"docs/usage.html#passing-parameters-to-sql-queries>`_"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:310
msgid ""
"`Advanced parameter types <http://initd.org/psycopg/docs/"
"usage.html#adaptation-of-python-values-to-sql-types>`_"
msgstr ""
"`Murakkab parametr turlari <http://initd.org/psycopg/docs/"
"usage.html#adaptation-of-python-values-to-sql-types>`_"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:311
msgid "`Psycopg documentation <https://www.psycopg.org/docs/sql.html>`_"
msgstr "`Psycopg hujjatlari <https://www.psycopg.org/docs/sql.html>`_"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:314
msgid "Building the domains"
msgstr "Domain'larni qurish"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:316
msgid ""
"Domains are represented as lists and are serializable. You would be tented "
"to manipulate these lists directly, however it can introduce subtle issues "
"where the user could inject a domain if the input is not normalized. "
"Use :class:`~odoo.fields.Domain` to handle safely the manipulation of "
"domains."
msgstr ""
"Domain'lar ro'yxat shaklida ifodalanadi va serializatsiya qilinadi. Bu "
"ro'yxatlarni bevosita o'zgartirish istagi paydo bo'lishi mumkin, ammo bu "
"ko'zga tashlanmaydigan muammolarni keltirib chiqaradi: agar kirish qiymati "
"normallashtirilmasa, foydalanuvchi domain inject qilishi mumkin. Domain'lar "
"bilan ishlashni xavfsiz bajarish uchun :class:`~odoo.fields.Domain` dan "
"foydalaning."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:338
msgid "Unescaped field content"
msgstr "Escape qilinmagan field kontenti"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:340
msgid ""
"When rendering content using JavaScript and XML, one may be tempted to use a "
"``t-raw`` to display rich-text content. This should be avoided as a frequent "
"`XSS <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross-site_scripting>`_ vector."
msgstr ""
"JavaScript va XML yordamida kontentni render qilganda rich-text kontentni "
"ko'rsatish uchun ``t-raw`` ishlatish istagi paydo bo'lishi mumkin. Bundan "
"qochish kerak, chunki bu keng tarqalgan `XSS <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Cross-site_scripting>`_ vektori."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:344
msgid ""
"It is very hard to control the integrity of the data from the computation "
"until the final integration in the browser DOM. A ``t-raw`` that is "
"correctly escaped at the time of introduction may no longer be safe at the "
"next bugfix or refactoring."
msgstr ""
"Ma'lumot yaxlitligini hisoblash paytidan brauzer DOM'iga oxirgi "
"integratsiyasigacha nazorat qilish juda qiyin. Kiritilgan paytda to'g'ri "
"escape qilingan ``t-raw`` keyingi bugfix yoki refactoring'dan so'ng endi "
"xavfsiz bo'lmasligi mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:361
msgid ""
"The above code may feel safe as the message content is controlled but is a "
"bad practice that may lead to unexpected security vulnerabilities once this "
"code evolves in the future."
msgstr ""
"Yuqoridagi kod xavfsizdek ko'rinishi mumkin, chunki xabar kontenti nazorat "
"ostida; ammo bu yomon amaliyot bo'lib, kelajakda kod rivojlanganda "
"kutilmagan xavfsizlik zaifliklariga olib kelishi mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:373
msgid ""
"While formatting the template differently would prevent such vulnerabilities."
msgstr ""
"Template'ni boshqacha formatlash esa bunday zaifliklarning oldini oladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:398
msgid "Creating safe content using :class:`~markupsafe.Markup`"
msgstr ":class:`~markupsafe.Markup` yordamida xavfsiz kontent yaratish"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:400
msgid ""
"See the `official documentation <https://markupsafe.palletsprojects.com/>`_ "
"for explanations, but the big advantage of :class:`~markupsafe.Markup` is "
"that it's a very rich type overrinding :class:`str` operations to "
"*automatically escape parameters*."
msgstr ""
"Tushuntirishlar uchun `rasmiy hujjatlar <https://"
"markupsafe.palletsprojects.com/>`_ ni ko'ring; :class:`~markupsafe.Markup` "
"ning katta afzalligi shundaki, u :class:`str` operatsiyalarini override "
"qiladigan juda boy tur bo'lib, *parametrlarni avtomatik escape qiladi*."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:405
msgid ""
"This means that it's easy to create *safe* html snippets by "
"using :class:`~markupsafe.Markup` on a string literal and \"formatting in\" "
"user-provided (and thus potentially unsafe) content:"
msgstr ""
"Ya'ni satr literaliga :class:`~markupsafe.Markup` ni qo'llab va "
"foydalanuvchi bergan (demak, potentsial xavfli) kontentni \"formatlab "
"kiritib\" *xavfsiz* html parchalarini yaratish oson:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:416
msgid ""
"though it is a very good thing, note that the effects can be odd at times:"
msgstr ""
"bu juda yaxshi narsa bo'lsa-da, ba'zan natijalar g'alati bo'lishi "
"mumkinligini yodda tuting:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:429
msgid ""
"Most of the content-safe APIs actually return a :class:`~markupsafe.Markup` "
"with all that implies."
msgstr ""
"Kontent bo'yicha xavfsiz API'larning ko'pchiligi "
"aslida :class:`~markupsafe.Markup` qaytaradi — bu bilan bog'liq barcha "
"oqibatlari bilan."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:432
msgid ""
"The :class:`~markupsafe.escape` method (and its "
"alias :class:`~odoo.tools.misc.html_escape`) turns a `str` into "
"a :class:`~markupsafe.Markup` and escapes its content. It will not escape "
"the content of a :class:`~markupsafe.Markup` object."
msgstr ""
":class:`~markupsafe.escape` method'i (va uning "
"alias'i :class:`~odoo.tools.misc.html_escape`) `str` "
"ni :class:`~markupsafe.Markup` ga aylantiradi va uning kontentini escape "
"qiladi. U :class:`~markupsafe.Markup` obyektining kontentini escape qilmaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:451
msgid ""
"When generating HTML code, it is important to separate the structure (tags) "
"from the content (text)."
msgstr ""
"HTML kod generatsiya qilganda strukturani (tag'larni) kontentdan (matndan) "
"ajratish muhim."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:478
msgid ""
"When working with translations, it is especially important to separate the "
"HTML from the text. The translation methods accepts "
"a :class:`~markupsafe.Markup` parameters and will escape the translation if "
"it gets receives at least one."
msgstr ""
"Tarjimalar bilan ishlaganda HTML'ni matndan ajratish ayniqsa muhim. Tarjima "
"method'lari :class:`~markupsafe.Markup` parametrlarini qabul qiladi va agar "
"kamida bittasini olsa, tarjimani escape qiladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:495
msgid "Escaping vs Sanitizing"
msgstr "Escaping va Sanitizing"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:499
msgid ""
"Escaping is always 100% mandatory when you mix data and code, no matter how "
"safe the data"
msgstr ""
"Ma'lumot va kodni aralashtirganda escaping har doim 100% majburiy — ma'lumot "
"qanchalik xavfsiz bo'lishidan qat'i nazar"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:502
msgid ""
"**Escaping** converts *TEXT* to *CODE*. It is absolutely mandatory to do it "
"every time you mix *DATA/TEXT* with *CODE* (e.g. generating HTML or python "
"code to be evaluated inside a `safe_eval`), because *CODE* always requires "
"*TEXT* to be encoded. It is critical for security, but it's also a question "
"of correctness. Even when there is no security risk (because the text is "
"100% guarantee to be safe or trusted), it is still required (e.g. to avoid "
"breaking the layout in generated HTML)."
msgstr ""
"**Escaping** *TEXT* ni *CODE* ga aylantiradi. Siz *DATA/TEXT* ni *CODE* "
"bilan aralashtirgan har bir holatda buni bajarish mutlaqo majburiy (masalan, "
"`safe_eval` ichida hisoblanadigan HTML yoki python kod generatsiya "
"qilganda), chunki *CODE* har doim *TEXT* kodlangan bo'lishini talab qiladi. "
"Bu xavfsizlik uchun juda muhim, shu bilan birga to'g'rilik masalasi hamdir. "
"Hatto xavfsizlik xatari bo'lmaganda ham (chunki matn 100% xavfsiz yoki "
"ishonchli ekani kafolatlangan), bu talab kuchda qoladi (masalan, generatsiya "
"qilingan HTML'da layout buzilmasligi uchun)."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:510
msgid ""
"Escaping will never break any feature, as long as the developer identifies "
"which variable contains *TEXT* and which contains *CODE*."
msgstr ""
"Dasturchi qaysi o'zgaruvchi *TEXT*, qaysi biri *CODE* saqlashini aniqlab "
"olsa, escaping hech qachon hech qanday funksiyani buzmaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:526
msgid ""
"**Sanitizing** converts *CODE* to *SAFER CODE* (but not necessary *safe* "
"code). It does not work on *TEXT*. Sanitizing is only necessary when *CODE* "
"is untrusted, because it comes in full or in part from some user-provided "
"data. If the user-provided data is in the form of *TEXT* (e.g. the content "
"from a form filled by a user), and if that data was correctly escaped before "
"putting it in *CODE*, then sanitizing is useless (but can still be done). If "
"however, the user-provided data was **not escaped**, then sanitizing will "
"**not** work as expected."
msgstr ""
"**Sanitizing** *CODE* ni *SAFER CODE* ga aylantiradi (lekin bu majburiy "
"ravishda *safe* kod emas). U *TEXT* ustida ishlamaydi. Sanitizing faqat "
"*CODE* ishonchsiz bo'lganda kerak, chunki u to'liq yoki qisman foydalanuvchi "
"bergan ma'lumotdan keladi. Agar foydalanuvchi bergan ma'lumot *TEXT* "
"shaklida bo'lsa (masalan, foydalanuvchi to'ldirgan formadagi kontent) va u "
"ma'lumot *CODE* ichiga qo'yishdan oldin to'g'ri escape qilingan bo'lsa, "
"sanitizing keraksiz (lekin baribir bajarish mumkin). Ammo agar foydalanuvchi "
"bergan ma'lumot **escape qilinmagan** bo'lsa, sanitizing kutilganidek "
"**ishlamaydi**."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:545
msgid ""
"Sanitizing can break features, depending on whether the *CODE* is expected "
"to contain patterns that are not safe. That's why `fields.Html` and "
"`tools.html_sanitize()` have options to fine-tune the level of sanitization "
"for styles, etc. Those options have to be carefully considered depending on "
"where the data comes from, and the desired features. The sanitization safety "
"is balanced against sanitization breakages: the safer the sanitisation the "
"more likely it is to break things."
msgstr ""
"Sanitizatsiya funksiyalarni buzishi mumkin — bu *CODE* ichida xavfsiz "
"bo'lmagan pattern'lar bo'lishi kutilganiga bog'liq. Shu sababli "
"`fields.Html` va `tools.html_sanitize()` style'lar va boshqalar uchun "
"sanitizatsiya darajasini nozik sozlash imkonini beruvchi option'larga ega. "
"Bu option'larni ma'lumot qayerdan kelayotganiga va kerakli funksiyalarga "
"qarab ehtiyotkorlik bilan tanlash kerak. Sanitizatsiya xavfsizligi u "
"keltirib chiqaradigan buzilishlar bilan muvozanatlanadi: sanitizatsiya "
"qanchalik xavfsiz bo'lsa, biror narsani buzish ehtimoli shunchalik yuqori."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:562
msgid "Evaluating content"
msgstr "Kontentni hisoblash (evaluate qilish)"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:564
msgid ""
"Some may want to ``eval`` to parse user provided content. Using ``eval`` "
"should be avoided at all cost. A safer, sandboxed, "
"method :class:`~odoo.tools.safe_eval` can be used instead but still gives "
"tremendous capabilities to the user running it and must be reserved for "
"trusted privileged users only as it breaks the barrier between code and data."
msgstr ""
"Ba'zilar foydalanuvchi bergan kontentni parse qilish uchun ``eval`` "
"ishlatishni xohlashi mumkin. ``eval`` ishlatishdan har qanday holatda ham "
"voz kechish kerak. Uning o'rniga xavfsizroq, sandbox'langan "
"method :class:`~odoo.tools.safe_eval` ishlatilishi mumkin, lekin u ham uni "
"ishga tushirgan foydalanuvchiga juda katta imkoniyatlar beradi va kod bilan "
"ma'lumot o'rtasidagi to'siqni buzganligi uchun faqat ishonchli, imtiyozli "
"foydalanuvchilar uchun qoldirilishi lozim."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/security.rst:586
msgid "Parsing content does not need ``eval``"
msgstr "Kontentni parse qilish uchun ``eval`` kerak emas"

