#: ../../content/developer/reference/backend/testing.rst:301
msgid ""
"Testing Python code and JS code separately is very useful, but it does not "
"prove that the web client and the server work together.  In order to do "
"that, we can write another kind of test: tours.  A tour is a mini scenario "
"of some interesting business flow.  It explains a sequence of steps that "
"should be followed.  The test runner will then create a PhantomJs browser, "
"point it to the proper url and simulate the click and inputs, according to "
"the scenario."
msgstr ""
"Python kod va JS kodni alohida testlash juda foydali, lekin bu web client va "
"server birgalikda ishlashini isbotlamaydi. Buni tekshirish uchun boshqa "
"turdagi test yozishimiz mumkin: tour'lar. Tour — biror qiziqarli biznes "
"oqimining mini senariysi. U bajarilishi kerak bo'lgan qadamlar ketma-"
"ketligini tushuntiradi. So'ngra test runner PhantomJs browser'ini yaratadi, "
"uni kerakli url'ga yo'naltiradi va senariyga muvofiq click va kiritishlarni "
"simulyatsiya qiladi."

