#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend.rst:6
msgid "Web framework"
msgstr "Web framework"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:8
msgid ""
"Managing assets in Odoo is not as straightforward as it is in some other "
"apps. One of the reasons is that we have a variety of situations where some, "
"but not all of the assets are required. For example, the needs of the web "
"client, the point of sale app, the website or even the mobile application "
"are different. Also, some assets may be large, but are seldom needed: in "
"that case we may want them to be :ref:`loaded lazily (on demand) <frontend/"
"assets/lazy_loading>`."
msgstr ""
"Odoo'da asset'larni boshqarish ba'zi boshqa ilovalardagidek to'g'ridan-"
"to'g'ri emas. Buning sabablaridan biri shundaki, bizda asset'larning hammasi "
"emas, balki ba'zilari kerak bo'ladigan turli holatlar mavjud. Masalan, web "
"client, point of sale ilovasi, website yoki hatto mobil ilova ehtiyojlari "
"bir-biridan farq qiladi. Bundan tashqari, ba'zi asset'lar katta bo'lishi "
"mumkin, lekin kamdan-kam kerak bo'ladi: bunday holatda ularni :ref:`dangasa "
"(talab bo'yicha) yuklashni <frontend/assets/lazy_loading>` xohlashimiz "
"mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:16
msgid "Asset types"
msgstr "Asset turlari"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:18
msgid ""
"There are three different asset types: code (`js` files), style (`css` or "
"`scss` files) and templates (`xml` files)."
msgstr ""
"Uchta turli asset turi mavjud: kod (`js` fayllar), uslub (`css` yoki `scss` "
"fayllar) va template'lar (`xml` fayllar)."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:27
msgid "Code"
msgstr "Kod"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:22
msgid ""
"Odoo supports :ref:`three different kinds of javascript files<frontend/"
"js_modules>`. All these files are then processed (native JS modules are "
"transformed into odoo modules), then minified (if not in "
"`debug=assets` :ref:`mode <frontend/framework/assets_debug_mode>`) and "
"concatenated. The result is then saved as a file attachment. These file "
"attachments are usually loaded via a `<script>` tag in the `<head>` part of "
"the page (as a static file)."
msgstr ""
"Odoo :ref:`uch xil javascript fayl turini<frontend/js_modules>` qo'llab-"
"quvvatlaydi. Keyin bu fayllarning barchasi qayta ishlanadi (native JS "
"module'lar odoo module'lariga aylantiriladi), so'ngra minify qilinadi (agar "
"`debug=assets` :ref:`rejimida <frontend/framework/assets_debug_mode>` "
"bo'lmasa) va birlashtiriladi. Natija esa fayl ilovasi (attachment) sifatida "
"saqlanadi. Bu fayl ilovalari odatda sahifaning `<head>` qismidagi `<script>` "
"tegi orqali (statik fayl sifatida) yuklanadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:35
msgid "Style"
msgstr "Uslub"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:30
msgid ""
"Styling can be done with either `css` or `scss <https://sass-lang.com/>`_. "
"Like the javascript files, these files are processed (`scss` files are "
"converted into `css`), then minified (again, if not in "
"`debug=assets` :ref:`mode <frontend/framework/assets_debug_mode>`) and "
"concatenated. The result is then saved as a file attachment. They are then "
"usually loaded via a `<link>` tag in the `<head>` part of the page (as a "
"static file)."
msgstr ""
"Uslublashni `css` yoki `scss <https://sass-lang.com/>`_ bilan bajarish "
"mumkin. Javascript fayllari kabi, bu fayllar ham qayta ishlanadi (`scss` "
"fayllar `css`ga aylantiriladi), so'ngra minify qilinadi (yana, agar "
"`debug=assets` :ref:`rejimida <frontend/framework/assets_debug_mode>` "
"bo'lmasa) va birlashtiriladi. Natija esa fayl ilovasi sifatida saqlanadi. "
"Ular keyin odatda sahifaning `<head>` qismidagi `<link>` tegi orqali (statik "
"fayl sifatida) yuklanadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:38
msgid ""
"Templates (static `xml` files) are handled in a different way: they are "
"simply read from the file system whenever they are needed, and concatenated."
msgstr ""
"Template'lar (statik `xml` fayllar) boshqacha usulda ishlanadi: ular kerak "
"bo'lgan paytda shunchaki fayl tizimidan o'qiladi va birlashtiriladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:41
msgid ""
"Whenever the browser loads odoo, it calls the `/web/webclient/qweb/` "
"controller to fetch the :ref:`templates <reference/qweb>`."
msgstr ""
"Brauzer odoo'ni yuklaganda, :ref:`template'larni <reference/qweb>` olish "
"uchun `/web/webclient/qweb/` controller'ini chaqiradi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:44
msgid ""
"It is useful to know that in most cases, a browser only performs a request "
"the first time it loads a page. This is because each of these assets are "
"associated with a checksum, which is injected into the page source. The "
"checksum is then added to the url, which means that it is possible to safely "
"set the cache headers to a long period."
msgstr ""
"Ko'p hollarda brauzer so'rovni faqat sahifani birinchi marta yuklaganda "
"bajarishini bilish foydali. Buning sababi shundaki, bu asset'larning har "
"biri sahifa manbasiga kiritiladigan checksum bilan bog'langan. Keyin "
"checksum url'ga qo'shiladi, ya'ni cache header'larini uzoq muddatga xavfsiz "
"belgilash mumkin bo'ladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:53
msgid "Bundles"
msgstr "Bundle'lar"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:55
msgid ""
"Odoo assets are grouped by *bundles*. Each bundle (a *list of file paths* of "
"specific types: `xml`, `js`, `css` or `scss`) is listed in the :ref:`module "
"manifest <reference/module/manifest>`. Files can be declared using `glob "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glob_(programming)>`_ syntax, meaning that "
"you can declare several asset files using a single line."
msgstr ""
"Odoo asset'lari *bundle*'lar bo'yicha guruhlanadi. Har bir bundle (aniq "
"turlardagi *fayl yo'llari ro'yxati*: `xml`, `js`, `css` yoki "
"`scss`) :ref:`module manifest <reference/module/manifest>` ichida "
"ko'rsatiladi. Fayllarni `glob <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Glob_(programming)>`_ sintaksisi bilan e'lon qilish mumkin, ya'ni bitta "
"qatorda bir nechta asset faylini e'lon qilishingiz mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:61
msgid ""
"The bundles are defined in each module's :file:`__manifest__.py`, with a "
"dedicated `assets` key which contains a dictionary. The dictionary maps "
"bundle names (keys) to the list of files they contain (values). It looks "
"like this:"
msgstr ""
"Bundle'lar har bir module'ning :file:`__manifest__.py` faylida, dictionary "
"saqlaydigan maxsus `assets` kaliti bilan aniqlanadi. Dictionary bundle "
"nomlarini (kalitlar) ular o'z ichiga olgan fayllar ro'yxatiga (qiymatlar) "
"moslashtiradi. Bu quyidagicha ko'rinadi:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:83
msgid ""
"Here is a list of some important bundles that most odoo developers will need "
"to know:"
msgstr ""
"Quyida ko'pchilik odoo dasturchilari bilishi kerak bo'lgan ba'zi muhim "
"bundle'lar ro'yxati keltirilgan:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:86
msgid ""
"`web.assets_common`: this bundle contains most assets which are common to "
"the web client, the website and also the point of sale. This is supposed to "
"contain lower level building blocks for the odoo framework. Note that it "
"contains the :file:`boot.js` file, which defines the odoo module system."
msgstr ""
"`web.assets_common`: bu bundle web client, website va shuningdek point of "
"sale uchun umumiy bo'lgan ko'pchilik asset'larni o'z ichiga oladi. U odoo "
"framework'i uchun quyi darajadagi qurilish bloklarini saqlashi kutiladi. "
"E'tibor bering, u odoo module tizimini aniqlaydigan :file:`boot.js` faylini "
"o'z ichiga oladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:91
msgid ""
"`web.assets_backend`: this bundle contains the code specific to the web "
"client (notably the web client/action manager/views/static XML templates)"
msgstr ""
"`web.assets_backend`: bu bundle web client'ga xos kodni o'z ichiga oladi "
"(xususan web client/action manager/view'lar/statik XML template'lar)"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:94
msgid ""
"`web.assets_frontend`: this bundle is about all that is specific to the "
"public website: ecommerce, portal, forum, blog, ..."
msgstr ""
"`web.assets_frontend`: bu bundle ommaviy website'ga xos bo'lgan barcha "
"narsalarga tegishli: ecommerce, portal, forum, blog, ..."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:97
msgid ""
"`web.assets_unit_tests`: all javascript unit testing code (tests, helpers, "
"mocks)"
msgstr ""
"`web.assets_unit_tests`: barcha javascript unit test kodi (test'lar, "
"helper'lar, mock'lar)"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:102
msgid ""
"Typically, handling assets is simple: you just need to add some new files to "
"a frequently used bundle like `assets_common` or `assets_backend`. But there "
"are other operations available to cover some more specific use cases."
msgstr ""
"Odatda asset'lar bilan ishlash oddiy: siz shunchaki `assets_common` yoki "
"`assets_backend` kabi tez-tez ishlatiladigan bundle'ga bir nechta yangi fayl "
"qo'shishingiz kerak. Lekin yanada aniqroq foydalanish holatlarini qamrab "
"olish uchun boshqa amallar ham mavjud."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:106
msgid ""
"Note that all directives targeting a certain asset file (i.e. `before`, "
"`after`, `replace` and `remove`) need that file to be declared beforehand, "
"either in manifests higher up in the hierarchy or in ``ir.asset`` records "
"with a lower sequence."
msgstr ""
"E'tibor bering, muayyan asset fayliga qaratilgan barcha direktivalar (ya'ni "
"`before`, `after`, `replace` va `remove`) uchun o'sha fayl oldindan e'lon "
"qilingan bo'lishi kerak — yoki ierarxiyada yuqoriroq turgan manifest'larda, "
"yoki past sequence qiymatiga ega ``ir.asset`` record'larida."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:112
msgid "`append`"
msgstr "`append`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:114
msgid ""
"This operation adds one or multiple file(s). Since it is the most common "
"operation, it can be done by simply using the file name:"
msgstr ""
"Bu amal bir yoki bir nechta fayl qo'shadi. U eng ko'p uchraydigan amal "
"bo'lganligi uchun, uni shunchaki fayl nomidan foydalanib bajarish mumkin:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:123
msgid ""
"By default, adding a simple string to a bundle will append the files "
"matching the glob pattern at the end of the bundle. Obviously, the pattern "
"may also be directly a single file path."
msgstr ""
"Sukut bo'yicha, bundle'ga oddiy satr qo'shish glob namunasiga mos fayllarni "
"bundle oxiriga qo'shadi. Tabiiyki, namuna to'g'ridan-to'g'ri bitta fayl "
"yo'li ham bo'lishi mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:128
msgid "`prepend`"
msgstr "`prepend`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:130
msgid "Add one or multiple file(s) at the beginning of the bundle."
msgstr "Bundle boshiga bir yoki bir nechta fayl qo'shadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:132
msgid ""
"Useful when you need to put a certain file before the others in a bundle "
"(for example with css files). The `prepend` operation is invoked with the "
"following syntax: `('prepend', <path>)`."
msgstr ""
"Bundle ichida ma'lum bir faylni boshqalardan oldin joylashtirish kerak "
"bo'lganda foydali (masalan, css fayllar bilan). `prepend` amali quyidagi "
"sintaksis bilan chaqiriladi: `('prepend', <path>)`."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:143
msgid "`before`"
msgstr "`before`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:145
msgid "Add one or multiple file(s) before a specific file."
msgstr "Bir yoki bir nechta faylni ma'lum bir fayldan oldin qo'shadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:147
msgid ""
"Prepending a file at the beginning of a bundle might not be precise enough. "
"The `before` directive can be used to add the given file(s) right *before* "
"the target file. It is declared by replacing the normal path with a 3-"
"element tuple `('before', <target>, <path>)`."
msgstr ""
"Faylni bundle boshiga qo'shish yetarlicha aniq bo'lmasligi mumkin. `before` "
"direktivasi berilgan fayl(lar)ni target fayldan bevosita *oldin* qo'shish "
"uchun ishlatiladi. U oddiy path o'rniga 3 elementli tuple `('before', "
"<target>, <path>)` yozish bilan aniqlanadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:159
msgid "`after`"
msgstr "`after`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:161
msgid "Add one or multiple file(s) after a specific file."
msgstr "Bir yoki bir nechta faylni ma'lum bir fayldan keyin qo'shadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:163
msgid ""
"Same as `before`, with the matching file(s) appended right *after* the "
"target file. It is declared by replacing the normal path with a 3-element "
"tuple `('after', <target>, <path>)`."
msgstr ""
"`before` bilan bir xil, faqat mos fayl(lar) target fayldan bevosita *keyin* "
"qo'shiladi. U oddiy path o'rniga 3 elementli tuple `('after', <target>, "
"<path>)` yozish bilan aniqlanadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:174
msgid "`include`"
msgstr "`include`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:176
msgid "Use nested bundles."
msgstr "Ichma-ich joylashgan bundle'lardan foydalanish."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:178
msgid ""
"The `include` directive is a way to use a bundle in other bundles to "
"minimize the size of your manifest. In Odoo we use sub bundles (prefixed "
"with an underscore by convention) to batch files used in multiple other "
"bundles. You can then specify the sub bundle as a pair `('include', "
"<bundle>)` like this:"
msgstr ""
"`include` direktivasi manifest hajmini kamaytirish uchun bitta bundle'ni "
"boshqa bundle'lar ichida ishlatish usulidir. Odoo'da bir nechta boshqa "
"bundle'larda qo'llaniladigan fayllarni guruhlash uchun sub bundle'lardan "
"(kelishuvga ko'ra pastki chiziq bilan boshlanadigan) foydalanamiz. Keyin sub "
"bundle'ni `('include', <bundle>)` juftligi shaklida quyidagicha "
"ko'rsatishingiz mumkin:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:190
msgid "`remove`"
msgstr "`remove`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:192
msgid "Remove one or multiple file(s)."
msgstr "Bir yoki bir nechta faylni olib tashlaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:194
msgid ""
"In some cases, you may want to remove one or multiple files from a bundle. "
"This can be done using the `remove` directive by specifying a pair "
"`('remove', <target>)`:"
msgstr ""
"Ba'zi hollarda bundle'dan bir yoki bir nechta faylni olib tashlashni "
"xohlashingiz mumkin. Buni `remove` direktivasi yordamida `('remove', "
"<target>)` juftligini ko'rsatish orqali amalga oshirish mumkin:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:205
msgid "`replace`"
msgstr "`replace`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:207
msgid "Replace an asset file with one or multiple file(s)."
msgstr "Asset faylini bir yoki bir nechta fayl bilan almashtiradi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:209
msgid ""
"Let us say that an asset needs not only to be removed, but you also want to "
"insert your new version of that asset at the same exact position. This can "
"be done with the `replace` directive, using a 3-element tuple `('replace', "
"<target>, <path>)`:"
msgstr ""
"Aytaylik, asset'ni nafaqat olib tashlash kerak, balki uning yangi "
"versiyasini xuddi shu joyga qo'yishni ham xohlaysiz. Buni `replace` "
"direktivasi bilan, 3 elementli tuple `('replace', <target>, <path>)` "
"yordamida amalga oshirish mumkin:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:221
msgid "Loading order"
msgstr "Yuklanish tartibi"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:223
msgid ""
"The order in which assets are loaded is sometimes critical and must be "
"deterministic, mostly for stylesheets priorities and setup scripts. Assets "
"in Odoo are processed as follows:"
msgstr ""
"Asset'lar yuklanadigan tartib ba'zan juda muhim va deterministik bo'lishi "
"kerak — asosan stylesheet ustuvorliklari va sozlash skriptlari uchun. "
"Odoo'da asset'lar quyidagi tartibda qayta ishlanadi:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:227
msgid ""
"When an asset bundle is called (e.g. `t-call-assets=\"web.assets_common\"`), "
"an empty list of assets is generated"
msgstr ""
"Asset bundle chaqirilganda (masalan, `t-call-assets=\"web.assets_common\"`), "
"asset'larning bo'sh ro'yxati yaratiladi"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:230
msgid ""
"All records of type `ir.asset` matching the bundle are fetched and sorted by "
"sequence number. Then all records with a sequence strictly less than 16 are "
"processed and applied to the current list of assets."
msgstr ""
"Bundle'ga mos keladigan barcha `ir.asset` turidagi record'lar olinadi va "
"sequence raqami bo'yicha tartiblanadi. Keyin sequence qiymati 16 dan qat'iy "
"kichik bo'lgan barcha record'lar qayta ishlanadi va joriy asset'lar "
"ro'yxatiga qo'llaniladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:234
msgid ""
"All modules declaring assets for said bundle in their manifest apply their "
"assets operations to this list. This is done following the order of modules "
"dependencies (e.g. `web` assets is processed before `website`). If a "
"directive tries to add a file already present in the list, nothing is done "
"for that file. In other word, only the first occurrence of a file is kept in "
"the list."
msgstr ""
"O'z manifest'ida ushbu bundle uchun asset e'lon qilgan barcha modullar o'z "
"asset amallarini shu ro'yxatga qo'llaydi. Bu modullar bog'liqliklari "
"tartibida bajariladi (masalan, `web` asset'lari `website` dan oldin qayta "
"ishlanadi). Agar direktiva ro'yxatda allaqachon mavjud faylni qo'shishga "
"harakat qilsa, o'sha fayl uchun hech narsa qilinmaydi. Boshqacha aytganda, "
"faylning faqat birinchi uchrashi ro'yxatda saqlanadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:240
msgid ""
"The remaining `ir.asset` records (those with a sequence greater than or "
"equal to 16) are then processed and applied as well."
msgstr ""
"Qolgan `ir.asset` record'lari (sequence qiymati 16 dan katta yoki teng "
"bo'lganlari) ham keyin qayta ishlanadi va qo'llaniladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:243
msgid ""
"Assets declared in the manifest may need to be loaded in a particular order, "
"for example :file:`jquery.js` must be loaded before all other jquery scripts "
"when loading the lib folder. One solution would be to create "
"an :ref:`ir.asset <frontend/assets/ir_asset>` record with a lower sequence "
"or a 'prepend' directive, but there is another simpler way to do so."
msgstr ""
"Manifest'da e'lon qilingan asset'larni ma'lum tartibda yuklash kerak "
"bo'lishi mumkin, masalan lib papkasini yuklaganda :file:`jquery.js` boshqa "
"barcha jquery skriptlaridan oldin yuklanishi shart. Bir yechim — kichikroq "
"sequence yoki 'prepend' direktivasi bilan :ref:`ir.asset <frontend/assets/"
"ir_asset>` record'i yaratish, biroq buni amalga oshirishning yana bir "
"oddiyroq usuli bor."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:249
msgid ""
"Since the unicity of each file path in the list of assets is guaranteed, you "
"can mention any specific file before a glob that includes it. That file will "
"thus appear in the list before all the others included in the glob."
msgstr ""
"Asset'lar ro'yxatida har bir fayl yo'lining yakkaligi kafolatlanganligi "
"sababli, siz istalgan aniq faylni uni o'z ichiga oladigan glob'dan oldin "
"ko'rsatishingiz mumkin. Shunday qilib, o'sha fayl ro'yxatda glob'ga kiruvchi "
"barcha boshqa fayllardan oldin turadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:262
msgid ""
"A module *b* removing/replacing the assets declared in a module *a* will "
"have to depend on it. Trying to operate on assets that have yet to be "
"declared will result in an error."
msgstr ""
"*a* modulida e'lon qilingan asset'larni olib tashlaydigan/almashtiradigan "
"*b* moduli unga bog'liq bo'lishi kerak. Hali e'lon qilinmagan asset'lar "
"ustida amal bajarishga urinish xatoga olib keladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:269
msgid "Lazy loading"
msgstr "Lazy loading (kechiktirilgan yuklash)"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:271
msgid ""
"It is sometimes useful to load files and/or asset bundles dynamically, for "
"example to only load a library once it is needed. To do that, the Odoo "
"framework provides a few helper functions, located in :file:`@web/core/"
"assets`."
msgstr ""
"Ba'zan fayllarni va/yoki asset bundle'larini dinamik ravishda yuklash "
"foydali bo'ladi, masalan kutubxonani faqat kerak bo'lganda yuklash uchun. "
"Buning uchun Odoo framework :file:`@web/core/assets` ichida joylashgan bir "
"nechta yordamchi funksiyalarni taqdim etadi."

