msgstr "`name`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:330
msgid "Name of the asset record (for identification purpose)."
msgstr "Asset record'ining nomi (identifikatsiya uchun)."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:333
msgid "`bundle`"
msgstr "`bundle`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:333
msgid "Bundle in which the asset will be applied."
msgstr "Asset qo'llaniladigan bundle."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:345
msgid "`directive` (default= `append`)"
msgstr "`directive` (standart= `append`)"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:336
msgid ""
"This field determines how the `path` (and `target` if needed) will be "
"interpreted. Here is the list of available directives along with their "
"required arguments:"
msgstr ""
"Bu field `path` (va kerak bo'lsa `target`) qanday talqin qilinishini "
"belgilaydi. Quyida mavjud direktivalar va ular talab qiladigan argumentlar "
"ro'yxati keltirilgan:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:339
msgid "**append**: `path`"
msgstr "**append**: `path`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:340
msgid "**prepend**: `path`"
msgstr "**prepend**: `path`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:341
msgid "**before**: `target`, `path`"
msgstr "**before**: `target`, `path`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:342
msgid "**after**: `target`, `path`"
msgstr "**after**: `target`, `path`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:343
msgid "**include**: `path` (interpreted as a **bundle name**)"
msgstr "**include**: `path` (**bundle nomi** sifatida talqin qilinadi)"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:344
msgid "**remove**: `path` (interpreted as a **target asset** to remove)"
msgstr ""
"**remove**: `path` (olib tashlanadigan **target asset** sifatida talqin "
"qilinadi)"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:345
msgid "**replace**: `target`, `path`"
msgstr "**replace**: `target`, `path`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:353
msgid "`path`"
msgstr "`path`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:348
msgid "A string defining one of the following:"
msgstr "Quyidagilardan birini aniqlaydigan string:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:350
msgid "a **relative path** to an asset file in the addons file system;"
msgstr "addons fayl tizimidagi asset fayliga **nisbiy yo'l** (relative path);"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:351
msgid "a **glob pattern** to a set of asset files in the addons file system;"
msgstr "addons fayl tizimidagi asset fayllar to'plamiga **glob pattern**;"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:352
msgid "a **URL** to an attachment or external asset file;"
msgstr "attachment yoki tashqi asset fayliga **URL**;"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:353
msgid "a **bundle name**, when using the `include` directive."
msgstr "`include` direktivasidan foydalanilganda **bundle nomi**."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:357
msgid "`target`"
msgstr "`target`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:356
msgid ""
"Target file to specify a position in the bundle. Can only be used with the "
"directives `replace`, `before` and `after`."
msgstr ""
"Bundle ichidagi joyni aniqlash uchun maqsadli fayl. Faqat `replace`, "
"`before` va `after` direktivalari bilan ishlatilishi mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:360
msgid "`active` (default= `True`)"
msgstr "`active` (default= `True`)"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:360
msgid "Whether the record is active"
msgstr "Record faol yoki yo'qligi"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:364
msgid "`sequence` (default= `16`)"
msgstr "`sequence` (default= `16`)"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:363
msgid ""
"Loading order of the asset records (ascending). A sequence lower than 16 "
"means that the asset will be processed *before* the ones declared in the "
"manifest."
msgstr ""
"Asset record'larining yuklanish tartibi (o'sish bo'yicha). 16 dan kichik "
"sequence asset manifest'da e'lon qilinganlardan *oldin* qayta ishlanishini "
"bildiradi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:368
msgid ""
"Note that the ``ir.asset`` use case is mainly for website-related "
"applications, as it allows for conditional assets (for example, when a style "
"option is enabled)."
msgstr ""
"E'tibor bering, ``ir.asset`` asosan website bilan bog'liq ilovalar uchun "
"ishlatiladi, chunki u shartli asset'larga imkon beradi (masalan, style "
"option yoqilganda)."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:372
msgid ""
"In such cases, the ``<asset id=\"...\">`` syntax should be preferred over "
"the ``<record id=\"...\" model=\"ir.asset\">`` syntax when defining the "
"record in XML."
msgstr ""
"Bunday hollarda XML'da record aniqlanayotganda ``<record id=\"...\" "
"model=\"ir.asset\">`` sintaksisi o'rniga ``<asset id=\"...\">`` sintaksisiga "
"ustunlik berilishi kerak."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/assets.rst:376
msgid "See :ref:`reference/data/asset`, especially about the ``active`` value."
msgstr ""
":ref:`reference/data/asset` ga qarang, ayniqsa ``active`` qiymati haqidagi "
"qismga."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:3
msgid "Error handling"
msgstr "Xatolarni boshqarish"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:5
msgid ""
"In programming, error handling is a complex topic with many pitfalls, and it "
"can be even more daunting when you're writing code within the constraints of "
"a framework, as the way you handle errors needs to mesh with the way the "
"framework dispatches errors and vice versa."
msgstr ""
"Dasturlashda xatolarni boshqarish ko'p tuzoqlarga ega murakkab mavzu, "
"framework cheklovlari ichida kod yozayotganda esa u yanada qiyinlashadi, "
"chunki sizning xatolarni boshqarish usuli framework xatolarni tarqatish "
"usuliga mos kelishi kerak va aksincha."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:10
msgid ""
"This article paints the broad strokes of how errors are handled by the "
"JavaScript framework and Owl, and gives some recommendations on how to "
"interface with these systems in a way that avoids common problems."
msgstr ""
"Bu maqolada JavaScript framework va Owl xatolarni qanday boshqarishi umumiy "
"tarzda tasvirlanadi hamda keng tarqalgan muammolardan qochish uchun bu "
"tizimlar bilan qanday ishlash bo'yicha ba'zi tavsiyalar beriladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:15
msgid "Errors in JavaScript"
msgstr "JavaScript'dagi xatolar"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:17
msgid ""
"Before we dive into how errors are handled in Odoo as well as how and where "
"to customize error handling behavior, it's a good idea to make sure we're on "
"the same page when it comes to what we mean exactly by \"error\", as well as "
"some of the peculiarities of error handling in JavaScript."
msgstr ""
"Odoo'da xatolar qanday boshqarilishi hamda xatolarni boshqarish xatti-"
"harakatini qanday va qayerda moslashtirish mumkinligiga o'tishdan oldin, "
"\"xato\" deganda aynan nimani tushunayotganimiz va JavaScript'da xatolarni "
"boshqarishning ba'zi o'ziga xosliklari bo'yicha bir xil tushunchaga ega "
"bo'lganimizga ishonch hosil qilish foydali."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:23
msgid "The `Error` class"
msgstr "`Error` class'i"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:25
msgid ""
"The first thing that may come to mind when we talk about error handling is "
"the built-in `Error` class, or classes that extend it. In the rest of this "
"article, when we refer to an object that is an instance of this class, we "
"will use the term *Error object* in italics."
msgstr ""
"Xatolarni boshqarish haqida gapirganda birinchi navbatda o'ylashimiz mumkin "
"bo'lgan narsa — o'rnatilgan `Error` class'i yoki uni kengaytiruvchi "
"class'lar. Maqolaning qolgan qismida shu class'ning instance'i bo'lgan "
"obyektga murojaat qilganda kursiv bilan *Error object* atamasini ishlatamiz."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:31
msgid "Anything can be thrown"
msgstr "Har qanday narsani throw qilish mumkin"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:33
msgid ""
"In JavaScript, you can throw any value. It is customary to throw *Error "
"objects*, but it is possible to throw any other object, and even primitives. "
"While we don't recommend that you ever throw anything that is not an *Error "
"object*, the Odoo JavaScript framework needs to be able to deal with these "
"scenarios, which will help you understand some design decisions that we've "
"had to make."
msgstr ""
"JavaScript'da siz har qanday qiymatni throw qilishingiz mumkin. Odatda "
"*Error object* throw qilinadi, biroq boshqa har qanday obyekt va hatto "
"primitiv qiymatlarni ham throw qilish mumkin. Biz *Error object* bo'lmagan "
"narsani throw qilishni tavsiya qilmasak-da, Odoo JavaScript framework bunday "
"holatlarni ham qayta ishlay olishi kerak — bu bizning ba'zi loyihalash "
"qarorlarimizni tushunishga yordam beradi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:39
msgid ""
"When instanciating an *Error object*, the browser collects information about "
"the current state of the \"call stack\" (either a proper call stack, or a "
"reconstructed call stack for async functions and promise continuations). "
"This information is called a \"stack trace\" and is very useful for "
"debugging. The Odoo framework displays this stack trace in error dialogs "
"when available."
msgstr ""
"*Error object* yaratilganda browser \"call stack\"ning joriy holati haqida "
"ma'lumot to'playdi (bu haqiqiy call stack yoki async function'lar va promise "
"davomlari uchun qayta tiklangan call stack bo'lishi mumkin). Bu ma'lumot "
"\"stack trace\" deb ataladi va debug qilish uchun juda foydali. Odoo "
"framework mavjud bo'lganda bu stack trace'ni xato dialoglarida ko'rsatadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:45
msgid ""
"When throwing a value that is not an *Error object*, the browser still "
"collects information about the current call stack, but this information is "
"not available in JavaScript: it is only available in the devtools console if "
"the error is not handled."
msgstr ""
"*Error object* bo'lmagan qiymat throw qilinganda browser joriy call stack "
"haqida ma'lumotni baribir to'playdi, lekin bu ma'lumot JavaScript'da mavjud "
"bo'lmaydi: agar xato ushlanmasa, u faqat devtools console'da ko'rinadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:50
msgid ""
"Throwing *Error objects* enables us to show more detailed information, which "
"a user will be able to copy/paste if needed for a bug report, but it also "
"makes error handling more robust as it allows us to filter errors based on "
"their class when handling them. Unfortunately, JavaScript does not have "
"syntactic support for filtering by error class in the catch clause, but you "
"can relatively easily do it yourself:"
msgstr ""
"*Error object* throw qilish bizga batafsilroq ma'lumot ko'rsatish imkonini "
"beradi — foydalanuvchi kerak bo'lsa uni bug hisoboti uchun nusxalab "
"joylashtira oladi. Shu bilan birga bu xatolarni boshqarishni ishonchliroq "
"qiladi, chunki xatolarni ularning class'iga qarab filtrlash imkonini beradi. "
"Afsuski, JavaScript'da catch bo'limida xato class'i bo'yicha filtrlash uchun "
"sintaktik qo'llab-quvvatlash yo'q, lekin buni o'zingiz ancha oson amalga "
"oshirishingiz mumkin:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:69
msgid "Promise rejections are errors"
msgstr "Promise rad etilishi ham xatodir"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:71
msgid ""
"During the early days of Promise adoption, Promises were often treated as a "
"way to store a disjoint union of a result and an \"error\", and it was "
"pretty common to use a Promise rejection as a way to signal a soft failure. "
"While it might seem like a good idea at first glance, browsers and "
"JavaScript runtimes have long started to treat rejected Promises the same "
"way as thrown errors in pretty much every way:"
msgstr ""
"Promise'lar qo'llanila boshlagan ilk davrlarda ular ko'pincha natija va "
"\"xato\"ning ajratilgan birlashmasini saqlash usuli sifatida qaralgan va "
"Promise'ni rad etish yumshoq muvaffaqiyatsizlikni bildirish uchun keng "
"ishlatilgan. Bu birinchi qarashda yaxshi g'oyaday ko'rinsa-da, browser'lar "
"va JavaScript runtime'lari allaqachon rad etilgan Promise'larni deyarli "
"barcha jihatlarda throw qilingan xatolar bilan bir xil ko'rib chiqishni "
"boshlagan:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:78
msgid ""
"throwing in an async function has the same effect as returning a Promise "
"that is rejected with the thrown value as its rejection reason."
msgstr ""
"async function ichida throw qilish, rad etish sababi sifatida throw qilingan "
"qiymat bilan rad etilgan Promise qaytarish bilan bir xil natija beradi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:80
msgid ""
"catch blocks in async functions catch rejected Promises that were awaited in "
"the corresponding try block."
msgstr ""
"async function'lardagi catch bloklari mos try blokida await qilingan rad "
"etilgan Promise'larni ushlaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:82
msgid "runtimes collect stack information about rejected promises."
msgstr ""
"runtime'lar rad etilgan promise'lar haqida stack ma'lumotini to'playdi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:83
msgid ""
"a rejected Promise that is not caught synchronously dispatches an event on "
"the global/window object, and if `preventDefault` is not called on the "
"event, browsers log an error, and standalone runtimes like node kill the "
"process."
msgstr ""
"sinxron ravishda ushlanmagan rad etilgan Promise global/window obyektida "
"event yuboradi va agar bu event uchun `preventDefault` chaqirilmasa, "
"browser'lar xatoni log qiladi, node kabi mustaqil runtime'lar esa process'ni "
"to'xtatadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:86
msgid ""
"the debugger feature \"pause on exceptions\" pauses when Promises are "
"rejected"
msgstr ""
"debugger'ning \"pause on exceptions\" imkoniyati Promise'lar rad etilganda "
"ham to'xtaydi"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:88
msgid ""
"For these reasons, the Odoo framework treats rejected Promises in the exact "
"same way as thrown errors. Do not create rejected promises in places where "
"you would not throw an error, and always reject Promises with *Error "
"objects* as their rejection reason."
msgstr ""
"Shu sabablarga ko'ra Odoo framework rad etilgan Promise'larni throw qilingan "
"xatolar bilan aynan bir xil ko'rib chiqadi. Xato throw qilmaydigan joylarda "
"rad etilgan promise'lar yaratmang va Promise'larni doim rad etish sababi "
"sifatida *Error object* bilan rad eting."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:94
msgid "`error` events are not errors"
msgstr "`error` event'lari xato emas"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:96
msgid ""
"With the exception of `error` events on the window, `error` events on other "
"objects such as `<media>`, `<audio>` `<img>`, `<script>` and `<link>` "
"elements, or XMLHttpRequest objects are not errors. For the purpose of this "
"article, \"error\" specifically refers only to thrown values and rejected "
"promises. If you need to handle errors on these elements or want them to be "
"treated as errors, you need to explicitly add an event listener for said "
"event:"
msgstr ""
"Window'dagi `error` event'lari bundan mustasno, boshqa obyektlardagi — "
"`<media>`, `<audio>` `<img>`, `<script>` va `<link>` element'lari yoki "
"XMLHttpRequest obyektlaridagi `error` event'lari xato emas. Bu maqola "
"doirasida \"xato\" faqat throw qilingan qiymatlar va rad etilgan "
"promise'larni bildiradi. Agar bu element'lardagi xatolarni boshqarish kerak "
"bo'lsa yoki ularni xato sifatida ko'rmoqchi bo'lsangiz, o'sha event uchun "
"aniq event listener qo'shishingiz kerak:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:114
msgid "Lifecycle of errors within the Odoo JS framework"
msgstr "Odoo JS framework ichidagi xatolarning hayot tsikli"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:116
msgid ""
"Thrown errors unwind their call stack to find a catch clause that can handle "
"them. The way an error is handled depends on what code is encountered while "
"unwinding the call stack. While there are a virtually infinite number of "
"places errors could be thrown from, there are only a few possible paths into "
"the JS framework's error handling code."
msgstr ""
"Throw qilingan xatolar o'zini boshqara oladigan catch bo'limini topish uchun "
"call stack'ni ochib chiqadi. Xato qanday boshqarilishi call stack "
"ochilayotganda qanday kodga duch kelinishiga bog'liq. Xatolar throw "
"qilinishi mumkin bo'lgan joylar amalda cheksiz bo'lsa-da, JS framework'ning "
"xatolarni boshqarish kodiga olib boradigan yo'llar juda kam."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:123
msgid "Throwing an error at the top-level of a module"
msgstr "Module'ning yuqori darajasida xato throw qilish"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:125
msgid ""
"When a JS module is loaded, the code at the top level of that module is "
"executed and may throw. While the framework might report these errors with a "
"dialog, module loading is a critical moment for the JavaScript framework and "
"some modules throwing errors might prevent the framework code from booting "
"entirely, so any error reporting at this stage is \"best effort\". Errors "
"thrown during module loading should however always at the very least log an "
"error message in the browser console. Because this type of error is "
"critical, there is no way for the application to recover and you should "
"write your code in such a way that it's impossible for the module to throw "
"during definition. Any error handling and reporting that does happen at this "
"stage is purely with the objective of helping you, the developer, fix the "
"code that threw the error, and we provide no mechanism to customize how "
"these errors are handled."
msgstr ""
"JS module yuklanganda o'sha module'ning yuqori darajasidagi kod bajariladi "
"va throw qilishi mumkin. Framework bu xatolarni dialog bilan xabar qilishi "
"mumkin bo'lsa-da, module yuklanishi JavaScript framework uchun juda muhim "
"bosqich va ba'zi module'lar xato throw qilishi framework kodining umuman "
"ishga tushishiga to'sqinlik qilishi mumkin, shuning uchun bu bosqichdagi har "
"qanday xato xabari \"imkon qadar\" tarzda bo'ladi. Shunga qaramay, module "
"yuklanishi vaqtida throw qilingan xatolar hech bo'lmasa browser console'ida "
"xato xabarini log qilishi kerak. Bu turdagi xato kritik bo'lganligi uchun "
"ilova tiklana olmaydi va kodingizni module aniqlanish vaqtida throw qilishi "
"mumkin bo'lmaydigan tarzda yozishingiz kerak. Bu bosqichda amalga "
"oshiriladigan har qanday xatolarni boshqarish va xabar qilish faqat sizga, "
"dasturchiga, xato throw qilgan kodni tuzatishda yordam berish maqsadida "
"qilinadi va biz bu xatolar qanday boshqarilishini moslashtirish uchun hech "
"qanday mexanizm taqdim etmaymiz."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:138
msgid "The error service"
msgstr "Error service"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:140
msgid ""
"When an error is thrown but never caught, the runtime dispatches an event on "
"the global object (`window`). The type of the event depends on whether the "
"error was thrown synchronously or asynchronously: synchronously thrown "
"errors dispatch an `error` event, and errors thrown from within an "
"asynchronous context as well as rejected Promises dispatch an "
"`unhandledrejection` event."
msgstr ""
"Xato throw qilinib, lekin hech qachon ushlanmasa, runtime global obyektda "
"(`window`) event yuboradi. Event turi xatoning sinxron yoki asinxron throw "
"qilinganiga bog'liq: sinxron throw qilingan xatolar `error` event'ini "
"yuboradi, asinxron kontekst ichida throw qilingan xatolar hamda rad etilgan "
"Promise'lar esa `unhandledrejection` event'ini yuboradi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:146
msgid ""
"The JS framework contains a service that is dedicated to handling these "
"events: the error service. When receiving one of these events, the error "
"service starts by creating a new *Error object* that is used to wrap the "
"error that was thrown; this is because any value can be thrown, and Promises "
"can be rejected with any value, including `undefined` or `null`, meaning "
"that it's not guaranteed that it contains any information, or that we can "
"store any information on that value. The wrapping *Error object* is used to "
"collect some information about the thrown value so that it can be used "
"uniformly in the framework code that needs to display information about "
"errors of any type."
msgstr ""
"JS framework bu event'larni boshqarishga bag'ishlangan service'ni o'z ichiga "
"oladi: error service. Bu event'lardan birini olganda error service avvalo "
"throw qilingan xatoni o'rash uchun yangi *Error object* yaratadi; buning "
"sababi shundaki, har qanday qiymat throw qilinishi mumkin va Promise'lar "
"`undefined` yoki `null` kabi har qanday qiymat bilan rad etilishi mumkin, "
"ya'ni uning biror ma'lumot saqlashi yoki bizning o'sha qiymatda ma'lumot "
"saqlashimiz kafolatlanmaydi. O'ralgan *Error object* throw qilingan qiymat "
"haqida ma'lumot to'plash uchun ishlatiladi, shunda u har qanday turdagi "
"xatolar haqida ma'lumot ko'rsatishi kerak bo'lgan framework kodida bir xilda "
"ishlatilishi mumkin bo'ladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:155
msgid ""
"The error service stores a complete stack trace of the thrown error on this "
"wrapper *Error object* and, when the debug mode is `assets`, uses the source "
"maps to add information in this stack trace about the source file that "
"contains the function of each stack frame. The position of the function in "
"the bundled assets is kept, as it can be useful is some scenarios. When "
"errors have a `cause`, this process also unwinds the `cause` chain to build "
"a complete composite stack trace. While the `cause` field on *Error objects* "
"is standard, some major browsers still do not display the full stack trace "
"of error chains. Because of this, we add this information manually. This is "
"particularly useful when errors are thrown within Owl hooks, more on that "
"later."
msgstr ""
"Error service throw qilingan xatoning to'liq stack trace'ini shu o'rovchi "
"*Error object*da saqlaydi va debug rejimi `assets` bo'lganda source "
"map'lardan foydalanib, bu stack trace'ga har bir stack frame'ining "
"function'ini o'z ichiga olgan manba fayl haqida ma'lumot qo'shadi. "
"Function'ning bundle qilingan asset'lardagi joyi ham saqlanadi, chunki u "
"ba'zi holatlarda foydali bo'lishi mumkin. Xatolarda `cause` bo'lganda, bu "
"jarayon to'liq birlashgan stack trace qurish uchun `cause` zanjirini ham "
"ochib chiqadi. *Error object*lardagi `cause` maydoni standart bo'lsa-da, "
"ba'zi yirik browser'lar hanuzgacha xato zanjirlarining to'liq stack "
"trace'ini ko'rsatmaydi. Shu sababli biz bu ma'lumotni qo'lda qo'shamiz. Bu "
"ayniqsa xatolar Owl hook'lari ichida throw qilinganda foydali — bu haqda "
"keyinroq batafsil."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:165
msgid ""
"Once the wrapper error contains all the required information, we start the "
"process of actually handling the error. To do this, the error service "
"successively calls all functions registered in the `error_handlers` "
"registry, until one of these functions returns a truthy value, which signals "
"that the error has been handled. After this, if `preventDefault` was not "
"called on the error event, and if the error service was able to add a stack "
"trace on the wrapper error object, the error service calls `preventDefault` "
"on the error event, and logs the stack trace in the console. This is "
"because, as previously mentioned, some browsers do not display error chains "
"correctly, and the default behaviour of the event is the browser logging the "
"error, so we simply override that behaviour to log a more complete stack "
"trace. If the error service was not able to collect stack trace information "
"about the thrown error, we do not call `preventDefault`. This can happen "
"when throwing non-error values: strings, undefined or other random objects. "
"In those cases, the browser logs the stack trace itself, as it has that "
"information but does not expose it to the JS code."
msgstr ""
"O'rovchi xato barcha kerakli ma'lumotni o'z ichiga olgach, biz xatoni "
"haqiqatan boshqarish jarayonini boshlaymiz. Buning uchun error service "
"`error_handlers` registry'sida ro'yxatdan o'tgan barcha function'larni ketma-"
"ket chaqiradi, toki ulardan biri truthy qiymat qaytarmaguncha — bu xato "
"boshqarilganini bildiradi. Shundan so'ng, agar error event uchun "
"`preventDefault` chaqirilmagan bo'lsa va error service o'rovchi error "
"obyektiga stack trace qo'sha olgan bo'lsa, error service error event uchun "
"`preventDefault` chaqiradi va stack trace'ni console'ga log qiladi. Buning "
"sababi, yuqorida aytilganidek, ba'zi browser'lar xato zanjirlarini to'g'ri "
"ko'rsatmaydi, event'ning standart xatti-harakati esa browser xatoni log "
"qilishidir, shuning uchun biz to'liqroq stack trace log qilish uchun o'sha "
"xatti-harakatni override qilamiz. Agar error service throw qilingan xato "
"haqida stack trace ma'lumotini to'play olmagan bo'lsa, biz "
"`preventDefault`ni chaqirmaymiz. Bu xato bo'lmagan qiymatlar — string'lar, "
"undefined yoki boshqa tasodifiy obyektlar throw qilinganda yuz berishi "
"mumkin. Bunday hollarda browser stack trace'ni o'zi log qiladi, chunki unda "
"bu ma'lumot mavjud, lekin u JS kodiga ochilmaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:181
msgid "The `error_handlers` registry"
msgstr "`error_handlers` registry'si"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:183
msgid ""
"The `error_handlers` registry is the main way to extend the way that the JS "
"framework handles \"generic\" errors. Generic errors, in this context, means "
"errors that can happen in many places, but that should be handled uniformly. "
"Some examples:"
msgstr ""
"`error_handlers` registry'si JS framework \"umumiy\" xatolarni qanday "
"boshqarishini kengaytirishning asosiy usulidir. Bu kontekstda umumiy xatolar "
"deganda ko'p joylarda yuz berishi mumkin, lekin bir xilda boshqarilishi "
"kerak bo'lgan xatolar tushuniladi. Ba'zi misollar:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:187
msgid ""
"UserError: when the user attempts to perform an operation that the python "
"code deems invalid for business reasons, the python code raises a UserError, "
"and the rpc function throws a corresponding error in JavaScript. This has "
"the potential to happen on any rpc anywhere, and we do not want developers "
"to have to handle this kind of error explicitly in all those places, and we "
"want the same behavior to happen everywhere: stop the currently executing "
"code (which is achieved by the throw), and display a dialog that explains to "
"the user what went wrong."
msgstr ""
"UserError: foydalanuvchi python kodi biznes sabablarga ko'ra noto'g'ri deb "
"hisoblaydigan amalni bajarishga urinsa, python kodi UserError chiqaradi va "
"rpc function JavaScript'da mos xatoni throw qiladi. Bu har qanday joydagi "
"har qanday rpc'da yuz berishi mumkin va biz dasturchilar bunday xatoni "
"barcha o'sha joylarda alohida boshqarishga majbur bo'lishini xohlamaymiz, "
"shuningdek hamma joyda bir xil xatti-harakat bo'lishini istaymiz: joriy "
"bajarilayotgan kodni to'xtatish (bunga throw orqali erishiladi) va "
"foydalanuvchiga nima xato ketganini tushuntiruvchi dialog ko'rsatish."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:194
msgid ""
"AccessError: same reasoning as for user errors: it can happen at any point "
"and should be displayed the same way regardless of where it happens"
msgstr ""
"AccessError: user error'lar bilan bir xil mulohaza: u har qanday nuqtada yuz "
"berishi mumkin va qayerda yuz berishidan qat'i nazar bir xil tarzda "
"ko'rsatilishi kerak"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:196
msgid "LostConnection: same reasoning again."
msgstr "LostConnection: yana o'sha mulohaza."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:199
msgid "Throwing an error in an Owl component"
msgstr "Owl component ichida xato throw qilish"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:201
msgid ""
"Registering or modifying Owl components is the main way in which you can "
"extend the functionality of the web client. As such, most errors that are "
"thrown are in one way or another thrown from an Owl component. There are a "
"few possible scenarios:"
msgstr ""
"Owl component'larni ro'yxatga olish yoki o'zgartirish — web client "
"funksionalligini kengaytirishning asosiy usuli. Shu sababli throw "
"qilinadigan xatolarning aksariyati u yoki bu tarzda Owl component'dan throw "
"qilinadi. Bir necha mumkin bo'lgan holatlar bor:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:205
msgid "Throwing in the component's setup or during rendering"
msgstr "Component'ning setup'ida yoki rendering vaqtida throw qilish"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:206
msgid "Throwing from within a lifecycle hook"
msgstr "Lifecycle hook ichidan throw qilish"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:207
msgid "Throwing from an event handler"
msgstr "Event handler'dan throw qilish"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:209
msgid ""
"Throwing an error from an event handler or a function or method called "
"directly or indirectly from an event handler means that neither Owl's code "
"nor the JS framework's code is in the call stack. If you don't catch the "
"error, it lands directly in the error service."
msgstr ""
"Event handler'dan yoki event handler'dan to'g'ridan-to'g'ri yoxud bilvosita "
"chaqirilgan function yoki method'dan xato throw qilish call stack'da na Owl "
"kodi, na JS framework kodi borligini bildiradi. Agar xatoni ushlamasangiz, u "
"to'g'ridan-to'g'ri error service'ga tushadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:214
msgid ""
"When throwing an error in a component's setup or during rendering, Owl "
"catches the error and goes up the component hierarchy, allowing components "
"that have registered error handlers with the `onError` hook to attempt to "
"handle the error. If the error is not handled by any of them, Owl destroys "
"the application as it is likely in a corrupted state."
msgstr ""
"Component'ning setup'ida yoki rendering vaqtida xato throw qilinganda Owl "
"xatoni ushlaydi va component ierarxiyasi bo'ylab yuqoriga ko'tariladi, "
"`onError` hook bilan error handler ro'yxatga olgan component'larga xatoni "
"boshqarishga urinish imkonini beradi. Agar xato ulardan hech biri tomonidan "
"boshqarilmasa, Owl ilovani yo'q qiladi, chunki u ehtimol buzilgan holatda "
"bo'ladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:221
msgid ""
"`Error handling in the Owl documentation <https://github.com/odoo/owl/blob/"
"master/doc/v2/reference/error_handling.md>`_"
msgstr ""
"`Owl hujjatlarida xatolarni boshqarish <https://github.com/odoo/owl/blob/"
"master/doc/v2/reference/error_handling.md>`_"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:223
msgid ""
"Inside Odoo, there are some places where we do not want the entire "
"application to crash in case of error, and so the framework has a few places "
"where it uses the `onError` hook. The action service wraps actions and views "
"in a component that handles errors. If a client action or view throws an "
"error during rendering, it attempts to go back to the previous action. The "
"error is dispatched to the error service so that an error dialog can be "
"shown regardless. A similar strategy is used in most places where the "
"framework calls into \"user\" code: we generally stop displaying the faulty "
"component an show an error dialog."
msgstr ""
"Odoo ichida xato yuz berganda butun ilovaning ishdan chiqishini "
"xohlamaydigan joylar bor, shuning uchun framework `onError` hook'dan "
"foydalanadigan bir necha joyga ega. Action service action'lar va view'larni "
"xatolarni boshqaradigan component ichiga o'raydi. Agar client action yoki "
"view rendering vaqtida xato throw qilsa, u oldingi action'ga qaytishga "
"harakat qiladi. Xato error service'ga yuboriladi, shunda baribir xato "
"dialogi ko'rsatilishi mumkin bo'ladi. Framework \"foydalanuvchi\" kodini "
"chaqiradigan ko'p joylarda shunga o'xshash strategiya qo'llaniladi: biz "
"odatda nosoz component'ni ko'rsatishni to'xtatamiz va xato dialogini "
"ko'rsatamiz."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:232
msgid ""
"When throwing an error inside of a hook's callback function, Owl creates a "
"new *Error object* that contains stack information about where the hook was "
"registered, and sets its cause as the originally thrown value. This is "
"because the stack trace of the original error contains no information about "
"which component registered this hook and where, it only contains information "
"about what called the hook. Because hooks are called by Owl code, most of "
"this information is *generally* not very useful for developers, but knowing "
"where the hook was registered and by which component is very useful."
msgstr ""
"Hook'ning callback function'i ichida xato throw qilinganda Owl hook qayerda "
"ro'yxatga olinganligi haqida stack ma'lumotini o'z ichiga olgan yangi *Error "
"object* yaratadi va uning cause'ini dastlab throw qilingan qiymat sifatida "
"belgilaydi. Buning sababi shundaki, asl xatoning stack trace'ida bu hook'ni "
"qaysi component va qayerda ro'yxatga olgani haqida ma'lumot yo'q, unda faqat "
"hook'ni nima chaqirgani haqida ma'lumot bor. Hook'lar Owl kodi tomonidan "
"chaqirilganligi uchun bu ma'lumotning ko'p qismi *odatda* dasturchilar uchun "
"unchalik foydali emas, lekin hook qayerda va qaysi component tomonidan "
"ro'yxatga olinganini bilish juda foydali."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:241
msgid ""
"When reading errors that mention \"OwlError: the following error occurred in "
"<hookName>\", make sure to read both parts of the composite stack trace:"
msgstr ""
"\"OwlError: the following error occurred in <hookName>\" deb eslatuvchi "
"xatolarni o'qiyotganda birlashgan stack trace'ning ikkala qismini ham "
"o'qishni unutmang:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:263
msgid ""
"The first highlighted line tells you which component registered the "
"`onMounted` hook, while the second highlighted line tells you which function "
"threw the error. In this case, a child component is calling a function it "
"received as prop from its parent, and that function is a method of the "
"parent component. Both pieces of information can be useful, as the method "
"could have been called by mistake by the child (or at a point in the "
"lifecycle where it shouldn't), but it could also be that the parent's method "
"contains a bug."
msgstr ""
"Birinchi ajratilgan qator sizga `onMounted` hook'ini qaysi component "
"ro'yxatga olganini, ikkinchi ajratilgan qator esa xatoni qaysi function "
"throw qilganini ko'rsatadi. Bu holatda child component o'zining parent'idan "
"prop sifatida olgan function'ni chaqiryapti va bu function parent "
"component'ning method'i. Ikkala ma'lumot ham foydali bo'lishi mumkin, chunki "
"method child tomonidan xato bilan (yoki lifecycle'ning kerak bo'lmagan "
"nuqtasida) chaqirilgan bo'lishi mumkin, ammo parent'ning method'ida bug "
"bo'lishi ham ehtimoldan holi emas."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:272
msgid "Marking errors as handled"
msgstr "Xatolarni boshqarilgan deb belgilash"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:274
msgid ""
"In the previous sections, we talked about two ways to register error "
"handlers: one is adding them to the `error_handlers` registry, the other is "
"using the `onError` hook in owl. In both cases, the handler has to decide "
"whether to mark the error as handled."
msgstr ""
"Oldingi bo'limlarda error handler'larni ro'yxatdan o'tkazishning ikki usuli "
"haqida gapirdik: biri ularni `error_handlers` registry'ga qo'shish, "
"ikkinchisi owl'dagi `onError` hook'idan foydalanish. Ikki holatda ham "
"handler xatoni handled deb belgilash yoki belgilamaslikni hal qilishi kerak."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:280
msgid "`onError`"
msgstr "`onError`"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:282
msgid ""
"In the case of a handler registered in Owl with `onError`, the error is "
"considered by Owl as handled unless you rethrow it. Whatever you do in "
"`onError`, the user interface is likely not synchronized with the state of "
"the application, as the error prevented owl from completing some work. If "
"you are unable to handle the error, you should rethrow it, and let the rest "
"of the code handle it."
msgstr ""
"Owl'da `onError` bilan ro'yxatdan o'tgan handler holatida, agar siz xatoni "
"qayta throw qilmasangiz, Owl uni handled deb hisoblaydi. `onError` ichida "
"nima qilsangiz ham, xato owl'ning ba'zi ishlarni tugatishiga to'sqinlik "
"qilgani uchun, foydalanuvchi interfeysi ehtimol application state'i bilan "
"sinxronlashmagan bo'ladi. Agar xatoni handle qila olmasangiz, uni qayta "
"throw qilishingiz va qolgan kod uni handle qilishiga yo'l berishingiz kerak."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:288
msgid ""
"If you don't rethrow the error, you need to change some state so that the "
"application can render again in a non-erroring way. At this point, if you "
"don't rethrow the error it will not be reported. In some cases this is "
"desirable, but in most cases, what you should do instead is dispatch this "
"error in a separate call stack outside of Owl. The easiest way to do this is "
"to simply create a rejected Promise with the error as its rejection reason:"
msgstr ""
"Agar xatoni qayta throw qilmasangiz, application xatosiz qayta render "
"qilishi uchun qandaydir state'ni o'zgartirishingiz kerak. Bu nuqtada, agar "
"xatoni qayta throw qilmasangiz, u haqida xabar berilmaydi. Ba'zi hollarda bu "
"maqsadga muvofiq, lekin ko'p hollarda buning o'rniga bu xatoni Owl'dan "
"tashqarida alohida call stack'da dispatch qilishingiz kerak. Buning eng oson "
"yo'li — xatoni rejection reason sifatida olgan rejected Promise yaratish:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:308
msgid ""
"This causes the browser to dispatch an `unhandledrejection` event on the "
"window, which causes the JS framework's error handling to kick in and deal "
"with the error, in most cases by opening a dialog with information about the "
"error. This is the strategy that is used internally by the action service "
"and dialog service to stop rendering broken actions or dialogs while still "
"reporting the error."
msgstr ""
"Bu brauzerni window'da `unhandledrejection` event'ini dispatch qilishga "
"majbur qiladi, natijada JS framework'ning error handling mexanizmi ishga "
"tushadi va xatoni hal qiladi — ko'p hollarda xato haqidagi ma'lumot bilan "
"dialog ochib. Bu strategiya action service va dialog service tomonidan ichki "
"tarzda ishlatiladi: buzilgan action yoki dialog'larni render qilishni "
"to'xtatib, ayni paytda xato haqida xabar berish uchun."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:315
msgid "Handler in the `error_handlers` registry"
msgstr "`error_handlers` registry'dagi handler"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:317
msgid ""
"Handlers that are added to the `error_handlers` registry can mark an error "
"as being handled in two ways, with different meanings."
msgstr ""
"`error_handlers` registry'ga qo'shilgan handler'lar xatoni handled deb ikki "
"xil usulda, turli ma'nolarda belgilashi mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:320
msgid ""
"The first way is that the handler can return a truthy value, this means that "
"the handler has processed the error and made something happen because the "
"error it received matched the type of error it is able to handle. This "
"generally means it has opened a dialog or notification to warn the user "
"about the error. This prevents the error service from calling the following "
"handlers with higher sequence number."
msgstr ""
"Birinchi usul — handler truthy qiymat qaytarishi; bu handler xatoni qayta "
"ishlaganini va olgan xatosi u handle qila oladigan xato turiga mos "
"kelganligi uchun biror natija yuzaga kelganini bildiradi. Odatda bu "
"foydalanuvchini xato haqida ogohlantirish uchun dialog yoki notification "
"ochilganini anglatadi. Bu error service'ning yuqori sequence raqamli keyingi "
"handler'larni chaqirishiga to'sqinlik qiladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:326
msgid ""
"The other way is to call `preventDefault` on the error event: this has a "
"different meaning. After deciding that it is able to handle the error, the "
"handler needs to decide if the error it received is something that is "
"allowed to happen during normal operation and if it is, it should call "
"`preventDefault`. This is generally applicable to business errors such as an "
"access errors or validation errors: users can share links with other users "
"to ressources to which they do not have acces, and users can attempt to save "
"a record that's in an invalid state."
msgstr ""
"Ikkinchi usul — error event'ida `preventDefault` ni chaqirish: bu boshqa "
"ma'noga ega. Xatoni handle qila olishini aniqlaganidan keyin handler olgan "
"xatosi normal ishlash davomida yuz berishi mumkin bo'lgan holat ekanini hal "
"qilishi kerak, va agar shunday bo'lsa, `preventDefault` ni chaqirishi lozim. "
"Bu odatda access error yoki validation error kabi biznes xatolariga "
"tegishli: foydalanuvchilar o'zlarida ruxsat yo'q resurslarga havolalarni "
"boshqa foydalanuvchilar bilan ulashishi mumkin, shuningdek foydalanuvchilar "
"noto'g'ri holatdagi record'ni saqlashga urinishi mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:334
msgid ""
"When not calling `preventDefault`, the error is treated as unexpected, any "
"such occurrence during a test causes the test to fail, as it's generally "
"indicative of defective code."
msgstr ""
"`preventDefault` chaqirilmaganda xato kutilmagan deb hisoblanadi; test "
"davomida bunday holatning yuz berishi testning muvaffaqiyatsiz bo'lishiga "
"olib keladi, chunki bu odatda nosoz kod belgisidir."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:340
msgid "Avoid throwing errors as much as possible"
msgstr "Iloji boricha xato throw qilishdan saqlaning"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:342
msgid ""
"Errors introduce complexity in many ways, here are some reasons why you "
"should avoid throwing them."
msgstr ""
"Xatolar ko'p jihatdan murakkablik keltiradi; ularni throw qilishdan nega "
"saqlanish kerakligining bir necha sababi quyida keltirilgan."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:346
msgid "Errors are expensive"
msgstr "Xatolar qimmatga tushadi"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:348
msgid ""
"Because errors need to unwind the callstack and collect information as they "
"do so, throwing errors is slow. Additionally, JavaScript runtimes are "
"generally optimized with the assumption that exceptions are rare, and as "
"such generally compiles the code with the assumption that it doesn't throw, "
"and fall back to a slower code path if it ever does."
msgstr ""
"Xatolar callstack'ni bo'shatishi va shu jarayonda ma'lumot to'plashi "
"kerakligi uchun xato throw qilish sekin kechadi. Bundan tashqari, JavaScript "
"runtime'lari odatda exception'lar kam uchraydi degan taxmin bilan "
"optimallashtirilgan, shuning uchun kodni throw qilmaydi deb hisoblab compile "
"qiladi va agar throw yuz bersa, sekinroq kod yo'liga o'tadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:355
msgid "Throwing errors makes debugging harder"
msgstr "Xato throw qilish debug qilishni qiyinlashtiradi"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:357
msgid ""
"JavaScript debuggers, like the one included in the Chrome and Firefox "
"devtools for example, have a feature that allows you to pause the execution "
"when an exception is thrown. You can also choose whether to pause only on "
"caught exceptions, or on both caught and uncaught exceptions."
msgstr ""
"JavaScript debugger'lari, masalan Chrome va Firefox devtools'ga kiritilgani, "
"exception throw qilinganda bajarilishni to'xtatib turish imkonini beruvchi "
"xususiyatga ega. Shuningdek, faqat caught exception'larda yoki caught va "
"uncaught exception'larning ikkalasida to'xtashni tanlashingiz mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:362
msgid ""
"When you throw an error inside of code that is called by Owl or by the "
"JavaScript framework (e.g. in a field, view, action, component, ...), "
"because they manage resources, they need to catch errors and inspect them to "
"decide whether the error is critical and the application should crash, or if "
"the error is expected and should be handled in a particular manner."
msgstr ""
"Owl yoki JavaScript framework tomonidan chaqiriladigan kod ichida xato throw "
"qilganingizda (masalan field, view, action, component ichida), ular "
"resurslarni boshqarganligi uchun xatolarni catch qilib tekshirishi kerak: "
"xato kritikmi va application crash bo'lishi kerakmi, yoki xato kutilganmi va "
"muayyan tarzda handle qilinishi kerakmi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:368
msgid ""
"Because of this, almost all errors that are thrown within JavaScript code "
"are caught at some point, and although they may be rethrown if they cannot "
"be handled, this means that using the \"pause on uncaught exceptions\" "
"feature is effectively useless while working within Odoo, as it always "
"pauses within the JavaScript framework code, instead of near the code that "
"threw the error originally."
msgstr ""
"Shu sababli, JavaScript kod ichida throw qilinadigan deyarli barcha xatolar "
"biror nuqtada catch qilinadi, va handle qilinmasa qayta throw qilinishi "
"mumkin bo'lsa-da, bu Odoo ichida ishlaganda \"pause on uncaught exceptions\" "
"xususiyatidan foydalanish amalda befoyda ekanini bildiradi, chunki u har "
"doim xatoni asli throw qilgan kod yonida emas, balki JavaScript framework "
"kodi ichida to'xtaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:374
msgid ""
"However, the \"pause on caught exceptions\" feature is still very useful, as "
"it pauses execution on every throw statement and rejected promise. This "
"allows the developer to stop and inspect the execution context whenever an "
"exceptional situation occurs."
msgstr ""
"Biroq \"pause on caught exceptions\" xususiyati hamon juda foydali, chunki u "
"har bir throw statement va rejected promise'da bajarilishni to'xtatadi. Bu "
"dasturchiga istisno holat yuz berganda to'xtab, execution context'ni "
"tekshirish imkonini beradi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:379
msgid ""
"However, this is only true assuming that exceptions are rarely thrown. If "
"exceptions are thrown routinely, any action within the page can cause the "
"debugger to stop the execution, and the developer might need to step through "
"many \"routine\" exceptions before they can get to the actual exceptional "
"scenario they are interested in. In some situations, because clicking the "
"play button in the debugger removes focus from the page, it may even make "
"the interesting throw scenario inaccessible without using the keyboard "
"shortcut for resuming execution which results in poor developer experience."
msgstr ""
"Ammo bu faqat exception'lar kam throw qilinadi deb hisoblanganda to'g'ri. "
"Agar exception'lar muntazam throw qilinsa, sahifadagi har qanday harakat "
"debugger'ni bajarilishni to'xtatishga majbur qilishi mumkin, va dasturchi "
"o'zini qiziqtirgan haqiqiy istisno holatga yetib borish uchun ko'plab "
"\"muntazam\" exception'lardan o'tishga majbur bo'lishi mumkin. Ba'zi "
"vaziyatlarda debugger'dagi play tugmasini bosish sahifadan fokusni olib "
"tashlagani uchun, bajarilishni davom ettirish uchun klaviatura yorliqlarini "
"ishlatmasdan qiziqtirgan throw holatiga umuman yetib bo'lmaydi, bu esa "
"dasturchi uchun yoqimsiz tajriba yaratadi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:389
msgid "Throwing breaks the normal flow of the code"
msgstr "Throw qilish kodning normal oqimini buzadi"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:391
msgid ""
"When throwing an error, code that looks like it should always execute may be "
"skipped, this can cause many subtle bugs and memory leaks. Here is a simple "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"Xato throw qilinganda, har doim bajarilishi kerakdek ko'rinadigan kod "
"o'tkazib yuborilishi mumkin, bu esa ko'plab sezilmas bug'lar va memory "
"leak'larga olib keladi. Oddiy misol:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:400
msgid ""
"In this block of code, we add an event listener to an event target, then "
"call a function which may dispatch events on that target. After the function "
"call, we remove the event listener."
msgstr ""
"Bu kod blokida biz event target'ga event listener qo'shamiz, so'ngra o'sha "
"target'da event dispatch qilishi mumkin bo'lgan funksiyani chaqiramiz. "
"Funksiya chaqirilgandan keyin event listener'ni olib tashlaymiz."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:404
msgid ""
"If `someFunction` throws, the event listener will never be removed. This "
"means that the memory associated with this event listener is effectively "
"leaked and will never be freed unless the eventTarget itself gets "
"deallocated."
msgstr ""
"Agar `someFunction` throw qilsa, event listener hech qachon olib "
"tashlanmaydi. Bu shu event listener bilan bog'liq xotira amalda leak "
"bo'lganini va eventTarget'ning o'zi deallocate qilinmaguncha hech qachon "
"bo'shatilmasligini bildiradi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:408
msgid ""
"On top of the memory being leaked, the handler still being attached means "
"that it may be called for events being dispatched for reasons other than the "
"call to `someFunction`. This is a bug."
msgstr ""
"Xotiraning leak bo'lishidan tashqari, handler hamon ulangan bo'lishi uni "
"`someFunction` chaqiruvidan boshqa sabablar bilan dispatch qilingan "
"event'lar uchun ham chaqirilishi mumkinligini bildiradi. Bu bug."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:412
msgid ""
"To account for this, one would need to wrap the call in a `try` block, and "
"the cleanup in a `finally` block:"
msgstr ""
"Buni hisobga olish uchun chaqiruvni `try` blokiga, tozalashni esa `finally` "
"blokiga o'rash kerak bo'ladi:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:424
msgid ""
"While this now avoids the problems mentioned above, not only does this "
"require more code, it also requires knowledge that the function may throw. "
"It would be unmanageable to wrap all code that may throw in a `try/finally` "
"block."
msgstr ""
"Bu yuqorida aytilgan muammolarni chetlab o'tsa-da, u nafaqat ko'proq kod "
"talab qiladi, balki funksiya throw qilishi mumkinligini bilishni ham talab "
"etadi. Throw qilishi mumkin bo'lgan barcha kodni `try/finally` blokiga "
"o'rash boshqarib bo'lmas ish bo'lardi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:429
msgid "Catching errors"
msgstr "Xatolarni catch qilish"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:431
msgid ""
"Sometimes, you need to call into code that is known to throw errors and you "
"want to handle some of these errors. There are two important things to keep "
"in mind:"
msgstr ""
"Ba'zan xato throw qilishi ma'lum bo'lgan kodni chaqirishingiz kerak bo'ladi "
"va bu xatolarning ba'zilarini handle qilishni xohlaysiz. Yodda tutish kerak "
"bo'lgan ikki muhim narsa bor:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:434
msgid ""
"Rethrow errors that are not the type of error you expect. This should "
"generally be done with and `instanceof` check"
msgstr ""
"Siz kutgan turdagi bo'lmagan xatolarni qayta throw qiling. Bu odatda "
"`instanceof` tekshiruvi bilan amalga oshiriladi"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:436
msgid ""
"Keep the try block as small as possible. This avoid catching errors that are "
"not the one you're trying to catch. Generally, the try block should contain "
"exactly *one* statement."
msgstr ""
"try blokini iloji boricha kichik saqlang. Bu siz catch qilishga urinmagan "
"xatolarni catch qilishdan saqlaydi. Odatda try bloki aynan *bitta* statement "
"dan iborat bo'lishi kerak."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:454
msgid ""
"While this is straightforward with try/catch, it's much easier to "
"accidentally wrap a much larger portion of code in a catch clause when "
"working with `Promise.catch`:"
msgstr ""
"try/catch bilan bu oddiy ko'rinsa-da, `Promise.catch` bilan ishlaganda "
"kodning ancha kattaroq qismini tasodifan catch clause ichiga o'rab qo'yish "
"osonroq:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:468
msgid ""
"In this example, the catch block is actually catching errors in the entire "
"then block, which is not what we want. In this particular example, because "
"we properly filter based on the error type, we're not swallowing the error, "
"but you can see that it may be much easier to do so if we're expecting a "
"single error type and decide not to have the instanceof check. Notice "
"however that unlike the previous example, the null isn't going through the "
"codepath that uses `someVal`. To avoid this, catch clauses should generally "
"be as close as possible to the promise that may throw, and should always "
"filter on the error type."
msgstr ""
"Bu misolda catch bloki aslida butun then bloki ichidagi xatolarni catch "
"qilmoqda, bu esa biz xohlagan narsa emas. Aynan bu misolda xato turi "
"bo'yicha to'g'ri filtrlaganimiz uchun xatoni yashirmayapmiz, lekin agar "
"bitta xato turini kutayotgan bo'lsak va instanceof tekshiruvini qo'ymaslikka "
"qaror qilsak, buni qilish ancha oson bo'lishini ko'rish mumkin. Shuni ham "
"e'tiborga oling: oldingi misoldan farqli, null bu yerda `someVal` dan "
"foydalanuvchi kod yo'lidan o'tmaydi. Bundan saqlanish uchun catch clause'lar "
"odatda throw qilishi mumkin bo'lgan promise'ga iloji boricha yaqin bo'lishi "
"va har doim xato turi bo'yicha filtrlashi kerak."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:478
msgid "Error free control flow"
msgstr "Xatosiz control flow"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:480
msgid ""
"For the reasons outlined above, you should avoid throwing errors for doing "
"routine things, and in particular, for control flow. If a function is "
"expected to be unable to complete its work on a regular basis, it should "
"communicate that failure without throwing an exception. Consider the example "
"code:"
msgstr ""
"Yuqorida keltirilgan sabablarga ko'ra, muntazam ishlar uchun, xususan "
"control flow uchun xato throw qilishdan saqlanishingiz kerak. Agar funksiya "
"o'z ishini muntazam ravishda tugatib bo'lmasligi kutilsa, u bu "
"muvaffaqiyatsizlikni exception throw qilmasdan yetkazishi lozim. Quyidagi "
"misol kodni ko'rib chiqing:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:497
msgid ""
"There are many things that are problematic with this code. First, because we "
"want the variable `someVal` to be accessible after the `try/catch` block, it "
"needs to be declared before that block, and it cannot be `const` since it "
"needs to be assigned after initialization. This hurts readability further "
"down the road as you now have to look out for this variable potentially "
"being reassigned later in the code."
msgstr ""
"Bu kodda muammoli bo'lgan ko'p narsa bor. Birinchidan, `someVal` "
"o'zgaruvchisi `try/catch` blokidan keyin ham mavjud bo'lishini xohlaganimiz "
"uchun uni o'sha blokdan oldin e'lon qilish kerak, va u `const` bo'la "
"olmaydi, chunki initialization'dan keyin qiymat berilishi lozim. Bu "
"keyinchalik o'qishga zarar yetkazadi, chunki endi bu o'zgaruvchi kodning "
"keyingi qismlarida qayta qiymat olishi mumkinligini kuzatib borishga to'g'ri "
"keladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:503
msgid ""
"Second, when we catch the error, we have to check that the error is actually "
"the type of error we were expecting to catch, and if not, rethrow the error. "
"If we don't do this, we might end up swallowing errors that were *actually* "
"unexpected instead of reporting them correctly, e.g. we could be catching "
"and swallowing a TypeError if the underlying code tries to access a property "
"on `null` or `undefined`."
msgstr ""
"Ikkinchidan, xatoni catch qilganimizda, u haqiqatan biz catch qilishni "
"kutgan xato turi ekanini tekshirishimiz kerak, aks holda xatoni qayta throw "
"qilishimiz lozim. Agar buni qilmasak, *haqiqatan* kutilmagan xatolarni "
"to'g'ri xabar qilish o'rniga yashirib qo'yishimiz mumkin, masalan, quyi kod "
"`null` yoki `undefined` da property'ga murojaat qilishga urinsa, "
"TypeError'ni catch qilib yashirib qo'yishimiz mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:509
msgid ""
"Lastly, not only is this very verbose, but it's easy to do this incorrectly: "
"if you forget to add the `try/catch`, you are likely to end up with a "
"traceback. If you add the `try/catch` block but forget to rethrow unexpected "
"errors, you are swallowing unrelated errors. And if you want to avoid having "
"to reassign the variable you may move the entire block that uses the "
"variable inside the `try` block. The more code you have inside your `try` "
"block, the more likely you are to catch unrelated errors, and swallow them "
"if you forgot to filter by error type. It also adds an indentation level to "
"the entire block, and you may even end up with nested `try/catch` blocks. "
"Lastly, it makes it harder to identify which line is actually expected to "
"throw the error."
msgstr ""
"Va nihoyat, bu nafaqat juda ko'p yozuvni talab qiladi, balki uni noto'g'ri "
"bajarish ham oson: agar `try/catch` qo'shishni esdan chiqarsangiz, ehtimol "
"traceback bilan yuzlashasiz. Agar `try/catch` blokini qo'shsangiz-u, "
"kutilmagan xatolarni qayta throw qilishni unutsangiz, aloqasiz xatolarni "
"yashirgan bo'lasiz. Agar o'zgaruvchiga qayta qiymat berishdan saqlanishni "
"xohlasangiz, o'zgaruvchidan foydalanuvchi butun blokni `try` bloki ichiga "
"ko'chirishingiz mumkin. `try` blokingiz ichida kod qancha ko'p bo'lsa, "
"aloqasiz xatolarni catch qilish ehtimoli shuncha yuqori, va xato turi "
"bo'yicha filtrlashni unutgan bo'lsangiz ularni yashirib qo'yasiz. Bu "
"shuningdek butun blokka bitta indentation darajasini qo'shadi, hatto ichma-"
"ich `try/catch` bloklariga ega bo'lib qolishingiz mumkin. Oxirida esa bu "
"qaysi qator haqiqatan xato throw qilishi kutilayotganini aniqlashni "
"qiyinlashtiradi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:520
msgid ""
"The following sections outline some alternative approaches you can use "
"instead of using errors."
msgstr ""
"Quyidagi bo'limlarda xatolardan foydalanish o'rniga qo'llash mumkin bo'lgan "
"bir necha muqobil yondashuv bayon etilgan."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:524
msgid "Return `null` or `undefined`"
msgstr "`null` yoki `undefined` qaytaring"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:526
msgid ""
"If the function returns a primitive or an object, you can generally use "
"`null` or `undefined` to signal that it was unable to do its intended job. "
"This suffices in most cases. The code ends up looking something like this:"
msgstr ""
"Agar funksiya primitive yoki object qaytarsa, odatda o'z vazifasini bajara "
"olmaganini bildirish uchun `null` yoki `undefined` dan foydalanishingiz "
"mumkin. Ko'p hollarda bu kifoya qiladi. Kod natijada shunday ko'rinishga "
"keladi:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:536
msgid "As you can see, this is much simpler."
msgstr "Ko'rib turganingizdek, bu ancha oddiy."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:539
msgid "Return an object or array"
msgstr "Object yoki array qaytaring"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:541
msgid ""
"In some cases, a value of `null` or `undefined` is part of the expected "
"return values. In those cases, you can instead return a wrapper object or a "
"two-element array that contains either the return value or the error:"
msgstr ""
"Ba'zi hollarda `null` yoki `undefined` qiymati kutilgan qaytarish "
"qiymatlarining bir qismi bo'ladi. Bunday holatlarda buning o'rniga qaytarish "
"qiymatini yoki xatoni o'zida saqlagan wrapper object yoki ikki elementli "
"array qaytarishingiz mumkin:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:553
msgid "Or with an array:"
msgstr "Yoki array bilan:"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:565
msgid ""
"When using a two-element array, it is advisable to have the error be the "
"first element, so that it is harder to ignore by mistake when destructuring. "
"One would need to explicitly add a placeholder or comma to skip the error, "
"whereas if the error is the second element, it is easy to simply destructure "
"only the first element and mistakenly forget to handle the error."
msgstr ""
"Ikki elementli array ishlatilganda xatoni birinchi element qilib qo'yish "
"tavsiya etiladi, shunda destructuring vaqtida uni adashib e'tiborsiz "
"qoldirish qiyinlashadi. Xatoni o'tkazib yuborish uchun ochiq-oydin "
"placeholder yoki vergul qo'shish kerak bo'ladi, holbuki xato ikkinchi "
"element bo'lsa, faqat birinchi elementni destructure qilib xatoni handle "
"qilishni adashib unutish oson."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:572
msgid "When to throw errors"
msgstr "Qachon xato throw qilish kerak"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:574
msgid ""
"The previous sections give many good reasons to avoid throwing errors, so "
"what are some examples of cases where throwing an error is the best course "
"of action?"
msgstr ""
"Oldingi bo'limlarda xato throw qilishdan saqlanish uchun ko'plab asosli "
"sabablar keltirilgan, unda xato throw qilish eng to'g'ri yo'l bo'lgan "
"holatlarga qanday misollar bor?"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:577
msgid ""
"Generic errors that can happen in many places but should be treated the same "
"everywhere; e.g., access errors can happen on basically any RPC, and we "
"always want to display information about why the user doesn't have access."
msgstr ""
"Ko'p joyda yuz berishi mumkin, lekin hamma yerda bir xil ishlanishi kerak "
"bo'lgan umumiy xatolar; masalan, access error deyarli har qanday RPC'da yuz "
"berishi mumkin va biz har doim foydalanuvchida nega ruxsat yo'qligi haqidagi "
"ma'lumotni ko'rsatishni xohlaymiz."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:580
msgid ""
"Some precondition that should always be fulfilled for some operation is not "
"fulfilled; e.g., a view couldn't be rendered because the domain is invalid. "
"These types of error are generally not intended to be caught anywhere and "
"signal that code is incorrect or data is corrupted. Throwing forces the "
"framework to bail out and prevents operating in a broken state."
msgstr ""
"Biror operatsiya uchun har doim bajarilishi kerak bo'lgan shart bajarilmagan "
"bo'lsa; masalan, domain noto'g'ri bo'lgani uchun view render qilinmadi. "
"Bunday turdagi xatolar odatda hech qayerda catch qilinishi ko'zda tutilmaydi "
"va kod noto'g'ri yoki ma'lumot buzilganini bildiradi. Throw qilish "
"framework'ni ishni to'xtatishga majbur qiladi va buzilgan holatda "
"ishlashning oldini oladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/error_handling.rst:585
msgid ""
"When traversing some deep data structure recursively, throwing an error can "
"be more ergonomic and less error prone than having to manually test for "
"errors and forward them through many levels of calls. This should be very "
"rare in practice, and needs to be weighed against all the disadvantages "
"mentioned in this article."
msgstr ""
"Chuqur ma'lumot strukturasini rekursiv aylanib chiqishda xato throw qilish "
"xatolarni qo'lda tekshirib, ko'p qatlamli chaqiruvlar orqali uzatishdan "
"ko'ra ergonomikroq va kamroq xatoga moyil bo'lishi mumkin. Amalda bu juda "
"kam uchrashi kerak va bu maqolada aytilgan barcha kamchiliklar bilan "
"taqqoslab tortilishi lozim."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/framework_overview.rst:3
msgid "Framework Overview"
msgstr "Framework haqida umumiy ma'lumot"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/framework_overview.rst:6
#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/mobile.rst:8
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Kirish"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/framework_overview.rst:8
msgid ""
"The Odoo Javascript framework is a set of features/building blocks provided "
"by the ``web/`` addon to help build odoo applications running in the "
"browser. At the same time, the Odoo Javascript framework is a single page "
"application, usually known as the *web client* (available at the url ``/"
"web``)."
msgstr ""
"Odoo Javascript framework — brauzerda ishlaydigan odoo application'larini "
"qurishga yordam berish uchun ``web/`` addon tomonidan taqdim etiladigan "
"xususiyatlar/qurilish bloklari to'plami. Shu bilan birga, Odoo Javascript "
"framework — bu single page application bo'lib, odatda *web client* deb "
"ataladi (``/web`` url manzilida mavjud)."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/framework_overview.rst:13
msgid ""
"The web client started as an application made with a custom class and widget "
"system, but it is now transitioning to using native javascript classes "
"instead, and Owl as a component system. This explains why both systems are "
"currently in use in the codebase."
msgstr ""
"Web client dastlab maxsus class va widget tizimi bilan yaratilgan "
"application sifatida boshlangan, ammo hozir uning o'rniga native javascript "
"class'lariga va component tizimi sifatida Owl'ga o'tmoqda. Shu sababli "
"hozirda codebase'da ikki tizim ham qo'llanilmoqda."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/framework_overview.rst:18
msgid ""
"From a high-level perspective, the web client is a single-page application: "
"it does not need to request a full page from the server each time the user "
"performs an action. Instead, it only requests what it needs and then "
"replaces/updates the current screen accordingly. Also, it manages the url to "
"keep it in sync with the current state."
msgstr ""
"Yuqori darajadan qaraganda, web client — single-page application: "
"foydalanuvchi har bir harakat qilganda serverdan to'liq sahifa so'rashi "
"shart emas. Buning o'rniga u faqat kerakli narsani so'raydi va so'ngra joriy "
"ekranni shunga mos ravishda almashtiradi/yangilaydi. Shuningdek, u url'ni "
"joriy state bilan sinxron saqlash uchun boshqaradi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/framework_overview.rst:24
msgid ""
"The javascript framework (all or some parts) is also used in other "
"situations, such as the Odoo website or the point of sale. This reference is "
"mostly focused on the web client."
msgstr ""
"Javascript framework (butunlay yoki ba'zi qismlari) boshqa holatlarda ham "
"ishlatiladi, masalan Odoo website yoki point of sale'da. Bu qo'llanma asosan "
"web client'ga qaratilgan."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/framework_overview.rst:30
msgid ""
"It is common in the Odoo ecosystem to see the words *frontend* and *backend* "
"as synonyms for the odoo website (public) and the web client, respectively. "
"This terminology is not to be confused with the more common use of browser-"
"code (frontend) and server (backend)."
msgstr ""
"Odoo ekotizimida *frontend* va *backend* so'zlarini mos ravishda odoo "
"website (ommaviy) va web client uchun sinonim sifatida ishlatish keng "
"tarqalgan. Bu terminologiyani brauzer kodi (frontend) va server (backend) "
"ma'nosidagi kengroq tarqalgan qo'llanishi bilan aralashtirmaslik kerak."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/framework_overview.rst:37
msgid ""
"In this documentation, the word *component* always refers to new Owl "
"components, and *widget* refers to old Odoo widgets."
msgstr ""
"Bu hujjatda *component* so'zi har doim yangi Owl component'lariga, *widget* "
"esa eski Odoo widget'lariga ishora qiladi."

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/framework_overview.rst:42
msgid "All new development should be done in Owl, if possible!"
msgstr "Iloji bo'lsa, barcha yangi ishlanmalar Owl'da bajarilishi kerak!"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/framework_overview.rst:45
msgid "Code structure"
msgstr "Kod tuzilishi"

#: ../../content/developer/reference/frontend/framework_overview.rst:47
