#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:248
msgid ""
"The value to assign to a field is not always a simple string and you might "
"need to compute it. It can also be used to optimize the insertion of related "
"values, or because a constraint forces you to add the related values in "
"batch. See ::ref:`Add X2many fields <tutorials/define_module_data/x2m>`."
msgstr ""
"Field'ga beriladigan qiymat har doim oddiy satr bo'lmaydi va uni hisoblash "
"kerak bo'lishi mumkin. Undan tashqari, related qiymatlarni kiritishni "
"optimallashtirish uchun yoki constraint sizni related qiymatlarni batch "
"tarzida qo'shishga majbur qilgani uchun ham foydalanish mumkin. "
"Qarang: ::ref:`X2many field'lar qo'shish <tutorials/define_module_data/x2m>`."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:261
msgid ""
"The offers you added should always be in a date relative to the installation "
"of the module."
msgstr ""
"Siz qo'shgan offer'lar har doim modul o'rnatilgan sanaga nisbatan "
"hisoblangan sanada bo'lishi kerak."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:267
msgid ""
"Sometimes, you need to call the ORM to do a ``search``. This is not feasible "
"with the CSV format."
msgstr ""
"Ba'zida ``search`` bajarish uchun ORM'ni chaqirish kerak bo'ladi. Buni CSV "
"formatida amalga oshirib bo'lmaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:280
msgid ""
"In this code snippet, it is needed because the master data depends on the "
"localization installed."
msgstr ""
"Bu kod parchasida bu zarur, chunki master data o'rnatilgan localization'ga "
"bog'liq."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:286
msgid "You might also need to execute python code when loading data."
msgstr ""
"Ma'lumotlarni yuklashda python kodini bajarish ham kerak bo'lishi mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:294
msgid ""
"Validate one of the demo data offers by using the \"Accept Offer\" button. "
"Refuse the others."
msgstr ""
"Demo data offer'laridan birini \"Accept Offer\" tugmasi yordamida "
"tasdiqlang. Qolganlarini rad eting."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:301
msgid "Add X2many fields"
msgstr "X2many field'lar qo'shish"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:303
msgid ""
"**Reference**: the documentation related to this topic can be found "
"in :class:`~odoo.fields.Command`."
msgstr ""
"**Manba**: bu mavzuga tegishli hujjatlarni :class:`~odoo.fields.Command` da "
"topishingiz mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:306
msgid ""
"If you need to add related data in a One2many or a Many2many field, you can "
"do so by using the :class:`~odoo.fields.Command` methods."
msgstr ""
"Agar One2many yoki Many2many field'ga related ma'lumot qo'shish kerak "
"bo'lsa, buni :class:`~odoo.fields.Command` method'lari yordamida "
"bajarishingiz mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:325
msgid ""
"Create one new Property, but this time with some offers created directly "
"inside the One2many field linked to the Offers."
msgstr ""
"Yana bitta yangi Property yarating, lekin bu safar Offers bilan bog'langan "
"One2many field ichida bir nechta offer bevosita yaratilgan holda."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:329
msgid "Accessing the data"
msgstr "Ma'lumotlarga murojaat qilish"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:331
msgid ""
"You should never access demo data outside of the demo data declaration, not "
"even in tests."
msgstr ""
"Demo data'ga hech qachon demo data e'lonidan tashqarida murojaat "
"qilmasligingiz kerak, hatto test'larda ham."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:334
msgid "There are multiple ways to access the master/demo data."
msgstr "Master/demo data'ga murojaat qilishning bir nechta yo'li bor."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:336
msgid ""
"In python code, you can use the ``env.ref(self, xml_id, "
"raise_if_not_found=True)`` method. It returns the recordset linked to the "
"``xml_id`` you specify."
msgstr ""
"Python kodida ``env.ref(self, xml_id, raise_if_not_found=True)`` method'idan "
"foydalanishingiz mumkin. U siz ko'rsatgan ``xml_id`` bilan bog'langan "
"recordset'ni qaytaradi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:339
msgid "In XML, you can use the `ref` key like this"
msgstr "XML'da `ref` kalitini quyidagicha ishlatishingiz mumkin"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:349
msgid ""
"It will call the ref method, and store the id of the record returned on the "
"field ``related_id`` of the record of type ``tutorial.example`` with id "
"``id1``."
msgstr ""
"U ref method'ini chaqiradi va qaytarilgan record'ning id'sini ``id1`` id'li "
"``tutorial.example`` turidagi record'ning ``related_id`` field'ida saqlaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:352
msgid ""
"In CSV, the title of the column must be suffixed with ``:id`` or ``/id``."
msgstr ""
"CSV'da ustun sarlavhasiga ``:id`` yoki ``/id`` qo'shimchasi qo'shilishi "
"shart."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:361
msgid ""
"In SQL, it is more complicated, see :ref:`the advanced section <tutorials/"
"define_module_data/xml_id>`."
msgstr ""
"SQL'da bu murakkabroq, :ref:`kengaytirilgan bo'limga <tutorials/"
"define_module_data/xml_id>` qarang."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:364
msgid ""
"Data can always be deleted by the user. Always code defensively, taking this "
"into account."
msgstr ""
"Ma'lumotlar foydalanuvchi tomonidan har doim o'chirilishi mumkin. Buni "
"hisobga olib, kodni har doim himoyalangan tarzda yozing."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:371
msgid "Advanced"
msgstr "Kengaytirilgan"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:376
msgid "What is the XML id?"
msgstr "XML id nima?"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:378
msgid ""
"Because we don't want a column ``xml_id`` in every single SQL table of the "
"database, we need a mechanism to store it. This is done with the "
"``ir.model.data`` model."
msgstr ""
"Ma'lumotlar bazasining har bir SQL jadvalida ``xml_id`` ustuni bo'lishini "
"istamaganimiz uchun, uni saqlash uchun mexanizm kerak. Bu ``ir.model.data`` "
"model'i yordamida amalga oshiriladi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:381
msgid ""
"It contains the name of the record (the ``xml_id``) along with the module in "
"which it is defined, the model defining it, and the id of it."
msgstr ""
"U record nomini (``xml_id``), shuningdek u aniqlangan module'ni, uni "
"aniqlaydigan model'ni va uning id'sini saqlaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:385
msgid "No update"
msgstr "Yangilanmaslik (noupdate)"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:387
msgid ""
"The records created with the ``noupdate`` flag won't be updated when "
"upgrading the module that created them, but it will be created if it didn't "
"exist yet."
msgstr ""
"``noupdate`` flag bilan yaratilgan record'lar ularni yaratgan module "
"yangilanganda o'zgartirilmaydi, lekin agar hali mavjud bo'lmasa, yaratiladi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:390
msgid ""
"``odoo-bin -i module`` will bypass this setting and always load the data. "
"But normally one shouldn't do this on a production database."
msgstr ""
"``odoo-bin -i module`` bu sozlamani chetlab o'tadi va ma'lumotlarni har doim "
"yuklaydi. Lekin odatda buni production ma'lumotlar bazasida qilmaslik kerak."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:403
msgid "Import as SQL"
msgstr "SQL sifatida import qilish"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:405
msgid ""
"In some cases, it makes sense to do the import directly in SQL. This is "
"however discouraged as it bypasses all the features of the ORM, computed "
"fields (including metadata) and python constraints."
msgstr ""
"Ba'zi hollarda import'ni to'g'ridan-to'g'ri SQL'da bajarish o'rinli bo'ladi. "
"Biroq bu tavsiya etilmaydi, chunki u ORM'ning barcha imkoniyatlarini, "
"computed field'larni (metadata bilan birga) va python constraint'larini "
"chetlab o'tadi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:408
msgid ""
"Generally using raw SQL also bypasses ACLs and increases the risks of "
"injections."
msgstr ""
"Umuman olganda, xom SQL'dan foydalanish ACL'larni ham chetlab o'tadi va "
"injection xavfini oshiradi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:410
msgid "**Reference**: :ref:`Security in Odoo<reference/security>`"
msgstr "**Manba**: :ref:`Odoo'da xavfsizlik<reference/security>`"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:412
msgid ""
"It can help to speed the import time by a lot `with huge files <https://"
"github.com/odoo/enterprise/blob/d46cceef8c594b9056d0115edb7169e207a5986f/"
"product_unspsc/hooks.py#L19>`__."
msgstr ""
"Bu `juda katta fayllar bilan <https://github.com/odoo/enterprise/blob/"
"d46cceef8c594b9056d0115edb7169e207a5986f/product_unspsc/hooks.py#L19>`__ "
"import vaqtini sezilarli darajada tezlashtirishga yordam beradi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:414
msgid ""
"For more complex imports like for the `translations <https://github.com/odoo/"
"odoo/blob/e1f8d549895cd9c459e6350430f30d541d02838a/odoo/addons/base/models/"
"ir_translation.py#L24>`__."
msgstr ""
"`Tarjimalar <https://github.com/odoo/odoo/blob/"
"e1f8d549895cd9c459e6350430f30d541d02838a/odoo/addons/base/models/"
"ir_translation.py#L24>`__ kabi murakkabroq import'lar uchun."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/define_module_data.rst:416
msgid ""
"It can be necessary to `initialize the database <https://github.com/odoo/"
"odoo/blob/e1f8d549895cd9c459e6350430f30d541d02838a/odoo/addons/base/data/"
"base_data.sql>`__."
msgstr ""
"`Ma'lumotlar bazasini ishga tayyorlash <https://github.com/odoo/odoo/blob/"
"e1f8d549895cd9c459e6350430f30d541d02838a/odoo/addons/base/data/"
"base_data.sql>`__ zarur bo'lishi mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/discover_js_framework.rst:13
msgid ""
"This two parts tutorial is designed to introduce you to the basics of the "
"web framework. Whether you are new to the framework or have some prior "
"experience, this tutorial will provide you with a solid foundation for using "
"the web framework in your projects."
msgstr ""
"Ikki qismdan iborat bu qo'llanma sizni web framework asoslari bilan "
"tanishtirish uchun mo'ljallangan. Framework bilan yangi tanishayotgan "
"bo'lsangiz ham, oldindan tajribangiz bo'lsa ham, bu qo'llanma "
"loyihalaringizda web framework'dan foydalanish uchun mustahkam poydevor "
"beradi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/discover_js_framework.rst:17
msgid ""
"The first part covers the basics of Owl components, which are a key part of "
"the web framework. Owl components are reusable UI components that can be "
"used to build complex web interfaces quickly and efficiently. We will "
"explore how to create and use Owl components in Odoo. Then, in the second "
"part of this tutorial, we focus on creating a dashboard using various "
"features of Odoo. Dashboards are an essential part of any web application, "
"and provide a nice starting point to use and interact with the Odoo codebase."
msgstr ""
"Birinchi qism web framework'ning muhim qismi bo'lgan Owl component'lari "
"asoslarini qamrab oladi. Owl component'lari - murakkab web interfeyslarni "
"tez va samarali qurish uchun ishlatiladigan, qayta foydalanishga yaroqli UI "
"component'laridir. Biz Odoo'da Owl component'larini qanday yaratish va "
"ishlatishni o'rganamiz. So'ngra, bu qo'llanmaning ikkinchi qismida Odoo'ning "
"turli imkoniyatlaridan foydalanib dashboard yaratishga e'tibor qaratamiz. "
"Dashboard'lar har qanday web ilovaning muhim qismi bo'lib, Odoo "
"codebase'idan foydalanish va u bilan ishlash uchun qulay boshlang'ich nuqta "
"bo'ladi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/discover_js_framework.rst:24
msgid ""
"This tutorial assumes that you have some basic knowledge of development with "
"Odoo in general (models, controllers, QWeb, ...). If you are new to Odoo, we "
"recommend that you start with the :doc:`/developer/tutorials/"
"server_framework_101` tutorial before proceeding with this one."
msgstr ""
"Bu qo'llanma sizda Odoo bilan ishlash bo'yicha umumiy asosiy bilimlar "
"(model'lar, controller'lar, QWeb va h.k.) borligini nazarda tutadi. Agar "
"Odoo bilan yangi tanishayotgan bo'lsangiz, bunga o'tishdan avval :doc:`/"
"developer/tutorials/server_framework_101` qo'llanmasidan boshlashni tavsiya "
"qilamiz."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/discover_js_framework.rst:30
msgid ""
"Each chapter of this tutorial is an independant project.  If you feel "
"comfortable with Owl, you can start directly with chapter 2."
msgstr ""
"Bu qo'llanmaning har bir bobi mustaqil loyihadir. Agar Owl bilan o'zingizni "
"erkin his qilsangiz, to'g'ridan-to'g'ri 2-bobdan boshlashingiz mumkin."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/discover_js_framework.rst:38
