#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:6
msgid ""
"This tutorial assumes familiarity with the :doc:`server_framework_101` "
"tutorial and the :doc:`define_module_data` tutorial."
msgstr ""
"Bu qo'llanma :doc:`server_framework_101` va :doc:`define_module_data` "
"qo'llanmalari bilan tanish bo'lishingizni nazarda tutadi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:9
msgid ""
"Although, as developers, we prefer to have the full power of Python to write "
"our modules, it is sometimes not possible to do so; typically on managed "
"hosting solutions which do not allow the deployment of custom Python code "
"like the `Odoo.com <https://www.odoo.com/start>`_ platform."
msgstr ""
"Dasturchilar sifatida modul'larimizni yozishda Python'ning to'liq "
"imkoniyatiga ega bo'lishni afzal ko'rsak-da, ba'zan bunday qilish imkonsiz "
"bo'ladi; odatda maxsus Python kodini joylashtirishga ruxsat bermaydigan "
"boshqariladigan hosting yechimlarida, masalan `Odoo.com <https://"
"www.odoo.com/start>`_ platformasida."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:14
msgid ""
"However, the flexible nature of Odoo is meant to allow customizations out of "
"the box. Whilst a lot is possible with :doc:`Studio </applications/studio>`, "
"it is also possible to define models, fields and logic in :doc:`XML Data "
"Files <define_module_data>`. This makes it easier to develop, maintain and "
"deploy these customizations."
msgstr ""
"Biroq Odoo'ning moslashuvchan tabiati sozlashlarni darhol amalga oshirishga "
"imkon berish uchun mo'ljallangan. :doc:`Studio </applications/studio>` bilan "
"ko'p narsa qilish mumkin bo'lsa-da, model'lar, field'lar va "
"logikani :doc:`XML ma'lumot fayllari <define_module_data>` ichida aniqlash "
"ham mumkin. Bu esa bunday sozlashlarni ishlab chiqish, qo'llab-quvvatlash va "
"joylashtirishni osonlashtiradi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:19
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, we will learn how to define models, fields and logic in "
"XML data files and bundle them into a module. These are sometimes called "
"*importable modules*, or *data modules*. We will also see the limitations of "
"this approach to module development."
msgstr ""
"Bu qo'llanmada XML ma'lumot fayllarida model'lar, field'lar va logikani "
"qanday aniqlash va ularni bitta modulga jamlashni o'rganamiz. Bunday "
"modul'lar ba'zan *importable modules* yoki *data modules* deb ataladi. "
"Shuningdek, modul ishlab chiqishning bu yondashuvi cheklovlarini ham ko'rib "
"chiqamiz."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:24
msgid "Problem statement"
msgstr "Masala bayoni"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:26
msgid ""
"Like in the :doc:`server_framework_101` tutorial, we will be working on Real "
"Estate concepts."
msgstr ""
":doc:`server_framework_101` qo'llanmasidagi kabi, biz Real Estate "
"tushunchalari ustida ishlaymiz."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:28
msgid ""
"Our goal is to create a new application to manage Real Estate properties in "
"a similar (albeit simpler) way to the :doc:`server_framework_101` tutorial. "
"We will define the models, fields and logic in XML data files instead of "
"Python files."
msgstr ""
"Maqsadimiz — :doc:`server_framework_101` qo'llanmasiga o'xshash (ammo "
"soddaroq) tarzda Real Estate ko'chmas mulklarini boshqarish uchun yangi "
"ilova yaratish. Model'lar, field'lar va logikani Python fayllari o'rniga XML "
"ma'lumot fayllarida aniqlaymiz."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:32
msgid ""
"At the end of this tutorial, we will be able to achieve the following in our "
"app:"
msgstr ""
"Bu qo'llanma oxirida ilovamizda quyidagilarga erishishimiz mumkin bo'ladi:"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:34
msgid "Manage Real Estate properties that are for sale"
msgstr "Sotuvga qo'yilgan Real Estate ko'chmas mulklarini boshqarish"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:35
msgid "Publish these properties on a website"
msgstr "Bu mulklarni websaytda e'lon qilish"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:36
msgid "Accept offers online from the website"
msgstr "Websayt orqali onlayn takliflarni qabul qilish"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:37
msgid "Invoice the buyer when the property is sold"
msgstr "Mulk sotilganda xaridorga hisob-faktura yozish"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:42
msgid ""
"Like in any development project, a clear structure makes it easier to manage "
"and maintain the code."
msgstr ""
"Har qanday ishlab chiqish loyihasida bo'lgani kabi, aniq struktura kodni "
"boshqarish va qo'llab-quvvatlashni osonlashtiradi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:44
msgid ""
"Unlike standard Odoo modules that use both Python and XML files, data "
"modules use only XML files. Therefore, it is expected that your work tree "
"will look something like this:"
msgstr ""
"Python va XML fayllarining ikkovidan foydalanadigan standart Odoo "
"modul'laridan farqli ravishda, data modul'lar faqat XML fayllardan "
"foydalanadi. Shu sababli ish daraxtingiz taxminan quyidagicha ko'rinishi "
"kutiladi:"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:62
msgid ""
"The only Python files you will have are the :file:`__init__.py` "
"and :file:`__manifest__.py` files. The :file:`__manifest__.py` file will be "
"the same as for any Odoo module, but will also import its models in the "
"`data` list."
msgstr ""
"Sizda mavjud bo'ladigan yagona Python fayllar — :file:`__init__.py` "
"va :file:`__manifest__.py`. :file:`__manifest__.py` fayli har qanday Odoo "
"moduli uchun bo'lgani kabi bo'ladi, biroq o'z model'larini `data` ro'yxatida "
"ham import qiladi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:66
msgid ""
"Remember to list files in the `data` section of :file:`__manifest__.py` in "
"order of dependency, typically starting with model files."
msgstr ""
":file:`__manifest__.py` faylining `data` bo'limida fayllarni bog'liqlik "
"tartibida sanashni yodda tuting — odatda model fayllaridan boshlanadi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:69
msgid ""
"The :file:`__init__.py` file is empty, but is required for Odoo to recognize "
"the module if you ever want to deploy your module in the classic way (by "
"adding it in an addons path). It is not strictly necessary for modules that "
"will be *imported*, but it is a good practice to keep it."
msgstr ""
":file:`__init__.py` fayli bo'sh, ammo modulingizni klassik usulda (addons "
"path'ga qo'shish orqali) joylashtirmoqchi bo'lsangiz, Odoo modulni tanib "
"olishi uchun u talab qilinadi. *Import qilinadigan* modul'lar uchun u qat'iy "
"zarur emas, biroq uni saqlab qolish yaxshi amaliyot hisoblanadi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:74
msgid "Deploying the module"
msgstr "Modulni joylashtirish"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:76
msgid ""
"To deploy the module, you will need to create a zip file of the module and "
"upload it to your Odoo instance. Make sure that the module "
"`base_import_module` is installed on your instance, then go to "
"the :menuselection:`Apps --> Import Module` and upload the zip file. You "
"must be in :ref:`developer mode <developer-mode>` to see the `Import Module` "
"menu item."
msgstr ""
"Modulni joylashtirish uchun uning zip faylini yaratib, Odoo instance'ingizga "
"yuklashingiz kerak. `base_import_module` moduli instance'ingizda "
"o'rnatilganiga ishonch hosil qiling, so'ng :menuselection:`Apps --> Import "
"Module` ga o'ting va zip faylni yuklang. `Import Module` menyu bandini "
"ko'rish uchun :ref:`developer mode <developer-mode>` da bo'lishingiz shart."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:81
msgid ""
"If you modify the module, you will need to create a new zip file and upload "
"it again, which will reload all the data in the module. Note however that "
"some operations are not possible, like changing the type of a field you "
"created previously. Data created by previous versions of the module (like "
"removed fields) will not be automatically deleted. In general, the simplest "
"way to handle this is to start with a fresh database or to uninstall the "
"module prior to uploading the new version."
msgstr ""
"Agar modulni o'zgartirsangiz, yangi zip fayl yaratib, uni qaytadan "
"yuklashingiz kerak bo'ladi — bu moduldagi barcha ma'lumotlarni qayta "
"yuklaydi. Biroq shuni yodda tuting: ba'zi amallar imkonsiz, masalan avval "
"yaratgan field'ingiz turini o'zgartirish. Modulning oldingi versiyalari "
"tomonidan yaratilgan ma'lumotlar (masalan olib tashlangan field'lar) "
"avtomatik o'chirilmaydi. Umuman olganda, buni hal qilishning eng oddiy usuli "
"— toza ma'lumotlar bazasidan boshlash yoki yangi versiyani yuklashdan oldin "
"modulni o'chirib tashlash."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:88
msgid "When uploading a module, the wizard will accept two options:"
msgstr "Modulni yuklashda wizard ikkita variantni qabul qiladi:"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:90
msgid ""
"`Force init`: if your module is already installed and you upload it again; "
"checking this option will force the update of all data marked as "
"`noupdate=\"1\"` in the XML files."
msgstr ""
"`Force init`: agar modulingiz allaqachon o'rnatilgan bo'lsa va uni qaytadan "
"yuklasangiz; bu variantni belgilash XML fayllarda `noupdate=\"1\"` deb "
"belgilangan barcha ma'lumotlarni majburan yangilaydi."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:92
msgid "`Import demo data`: self explanatory"
msgstr "`Import demo data`: nomidan ma'lum"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:94
msgid ""
"It is also possible to deploy the module using the :doc:`odoo-bin <../"
"reference/cli>` command line tool with the `deploy` command:"
msgstr ""
"Modulni :doc:`odoo-bin <../reference/cli>` buyruq qatori vositasi orqali "
"`deploy` buyrug'i bilan joylashtirish ham mumkin:"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:101
msgid ""
"This command also accepts the `--force` option, which is equivalent to "
"the :guilabel:`Force init` option in the wizard."
msgstr ""
"Bu buyruq `--force` option'ini ham qabul qiladi, u "
"wizard'dagi :guilabel:`Force init` variantiga teng."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:104
msgid ""
"Note that the user you use to deploy the module must have `Administration/"
"Settings` access rights."
msgstr ""
"E'tibor bering: modulni joylashtirish uchun foydalanayotgan foydalanuvchida "
"`Administration/Settings` kirish huquqlari bo'lishi kerak."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:108
#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/server_framework_101/02_newapp.rst:76
msgid "Create the following folders and files:"
msgstr "Quyidagi papka va fayllarni yarating:"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:110
msgid ":file:`/home/$USER/src/tutorials/estate/__init__.py`"
msgstr ":file:`/home/$USER/src/tutorials/estate/__init__.py`"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:111
msgid ":file:`/home/$USER/src/tutorials/estate/__manifest__.py`"
msgstr ":file:`/home/$USER/src/tutorials/estate/__manifest__.py`"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:113
msgid ""
"The :file:`__manifest__.py` file should only define the name and the "
"dependencies of our modules. The only necessary framework module for now is "
"``base`` (and ``base_import_module`` - although your module does not "
"*depend* on it strictly speaking, you need it to be able to import your "
"module)."
msgstr ""
":file:`__manifest__.py` fayli faqat modul'larimiz nomini va bog'liqliklarini "
"aniqlashi kerak. Hozircha zarur bo'lgan yagona framework moduli — ``base`` "
"(va ``base_import_module`` - qat'iy aytganda modulingiz unga *bog'liq* "
"bo'lmasa-da, modulingizni import qilish imkoniyati uchun u kerak)."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:118
msgid "Create a zip file of your module and upload it to your Odoo instance."
msgstr ""
"Modulingizning zip faylini yarating va uni Odoo instance'ingizga yuklang."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:121
msgid "Models and basic fields"
msgstr "Model'lar va asosiy field'lar"

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:123
msgid ""
"As you can imagine, defining models and fields in XML files is not as "
"straightforward as in Python."
msgstr ""
"Tasavvur qilganingizdek, XML fayllarda model'lar va field'larni aniqlash "
"Python'dagi kabi oson emas."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:125
msgid ""
"Since data files are read sequentially, you must define the elements in the "
"right order. For example, you must define a model before you can define a "
"field on that model, and you must define fields before adding them to a view."
msgstr ""
"Ma'lumot fayllari ketma-ket o'qilgani uchun element'larni to'g'ri tartibda "
"aniqlashingiz kerak. Masalan, biror model'da field aniqlashdan oldin o'sha "
"model'ni aniqlashingiz, field'larni esa view'ga qo'shishdan oldin "
"aniqlashingiz kerak."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:129
msgid "In addition, XML is simply much more verbose than Python."
msgstr "Bundan tashqari, XML Python'ga qaraganda ancha ko'p so'zli."

#: ../../content/developer/tutorials/importable_modules.rst:131
msgid ""
"Let's start by defining a simple model to represent a Real Estate property "
"in the `models` directory of our module."
msgstr ""
"Modulimizning `models` katalogida Real Estate ko'chmas mulkini ifodalovchi "
"oddiy model'ni aniqlashdan boshlaylik."

